COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[145,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nRead a book about the major and minor signs of the Day of Judgment.\nDo good deeds and call on others to do the same, as these two actions are inseparable.\nShare a message in which you warn your fellow Muslims about the wrongdoing, and remind them that a wrongdoer will not succeed in this life nor in the Hereafter.\nguid\nYour status with Allah commensurate with your acts of goodness and worship.\nAllah's promise never changes.\nThe wrongdoer will not succeed in this life nor in the Hereafter.\nrefl\nوَلِكُلّٖ دَرَجَٰتٞ مِّمَّا عَمِلُواْۚ\nMeaning: In accordance with their deeds, the one who did less evil will not be like the one who did a great deal of evil, and the follower will not be like the leader. Similarly, although those who attain reward and Paradise will share the success, triumph and admission to Paradise, there will be differences (in status) between them that are known only to Allah. But they will all be pleased with what the Lord gives them and will be content with it. Al-Saadi: 274.\nPractically speaking, what is the benefit of knowing that people in Paradise will be at different ranks?\nوَرَبُّكَ ٱلۡغَنِيُّ ذُو ٱلرَّحۡمَةِۚ\nAllah Has only enjoined righteous deeds upon His servants and forbidden them to do evil deeds, out of mercy toward them and in their best interests. He is independent of means and has no need of any of His creation; the obedience of the obedient is of no benefit to Him, just as the disobedience of the disobedient does not harm Him at all. Al-Saadi: 274.\nAllah describes Himself as the Free of need after he mentions the recompense of the believers and disbelievers. Why?\nإِن يَشَأۡ يُذۡهِبۡكُمۡ وَيَسۡتَخۡلِفۡ مِنۢ بَعۡدِكُم مَّا يَشَآءُ كَمَآ أَنشَأَكُم مِّن ذُرِّيَّةِ قَوۡمٍ ءَاخَرِينَ ١٣٣\nSince you understand that you will inevitably depart from this world as others did, and you will leave it for those who come after you, as those who came before you departed and left it for you, then why would you take it as a place to settle forever and establish yourself therein? Why would you forget that it is merely a place that you are passing through, not a place to abide in forever? Ahead of you there is another abode, one in which there are all types of blessings and joy, one which is free of all defects and imperfections. That is the abode for which the first and the last strive and aim. And how unfortunate is the one who is content with less than that, who chooses to have no aspirations and is content to be among the losers. Al-Saadi: 274.\nFor a wise person, what is the benefit in knowing about nations before him that vanished and were replaced by others?\nفَقَالُواْ هَٰذَا لِلَّهِ بِزَعۡمِهِمۡ وَهَٰذَا لِشُرَكَآئِنَاۖ فَمَا كَانَ لِشُرَكَآئِهِمۡ فَلَا يَصِلُ إِلَى ٱللَّهِۖ وَمَا كَانَ لِلَّهِ فَهُوَ يَصِلُ إِلَىٰ شُرَكَآئِهِمۡۗ سَآءَ مَا يَحۡكُمُونَ ١٣٦\nAllah named the devils \"partners\" since the polytheists obeyed them by committing acts of disobedience to Allah, and therefore, they associated them with Allah in the duty of obedience. Al-Qurtubi: 9/39.\nAllah names the devils (partners.) Why?\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ زَيَّنَ لِكَثِيرٖ مِّنَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ قَتۡلَ أَوۡلَٰدِهِمۡ شُرَكَآؤُهُمۡ لِيُرۡدُوهُمۡ وَلِيَلۡبِسُواْ عَلَيۡهِمۡ دِينَهُمۡۖ\nThe killing is ascribed to the partners even though they did not directly inflict it, but since they called for it and made it appealing, it became as if they actually had done it. Al-Qurtubi: 9/39.\nAn individual calls for an evil act, encourages others to do it and makes it appealing to them. Does that make him like the doer of this evil act?\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ زَيَّنَ لِكَثِيرٖ مِّنَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ قَتۡلَ أَوۡلَٰدِهِمۡ شُرَكَآؤُهُمۡ لِيُرۡدُوهُمۡ وَلِيَلۡبِسُواْ عَلَيۡهِمۡ دِينَهُمۡۖ وَلَوۡ شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ مَا فَعَلُوهُۖ فَذَرۡهُمۡ وَمَا يَفۡتَرُونَ ١٣٧\nThey used to kill their children by burying them alive, and offered them as sacrifices to their idols. Their (partners) were the devils or the priests who were serving the idols. (To lead them to destruction) which is their evident loss in this life and the Hereafter. Ibn Juzay: 1/287.\nFrom this verse, describe Allah's favor upon us with Islam.\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ زَيَّنَ لِكَثِيرٖ مِّنَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ قَتۡلَ أَوۡلَٰدِهِمۡ شُرَكَآؤُهُمۡ لِيُرۡدُوهُمۡ وَلِيَلۡبِسُواْ عَلَيۡهِمۡ دِينَهُمۡۖ وَلَوۡ شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ مَا فَعَلُوهُۖ فَذَرۡهُمۡ وَمَا يَفۡتَرُونَ ١٣٧\nThe (partners) here are the devils who call for this evil act and make it appealing; also, the executers among humans who pass it along from one generation to another. Indeed, they are all partners in this horrendous act and its consequences in the Hereafter. Ibn Atiyah: 2/349.\nWhen does one become a partner with the devil?\nwords\nمَكَانَتِكُمYour way\nعَاقِبَةُ الدَّارِThe best ultimate abode\nذَرَأَHe created\nالحَرثِThe crops\nلِيُردُوهُمTo lead them to destruction\nوَلِيَلبِسُواTo confuse them [in their faith]\nيَفتَرُونَThey invent through lies"],[146,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nAsk Allah for righteous children and to aid you in raising them in a righteous way.\nChoose a time when the needs of the poor become intense, and give charity to them, so that perhaps your reward is amplified.\nThank Allah after eating and drinking.\nguid\nMaking vows at the graves of righteous people and shrines is an action of polytheists, which is made appealing to ignorant Muslims by the devil.\nBirth prevention is an act from the pre-Islam age. It reflects a negative assumption about Allah.\nWastefulness is a censured trait which is disliked by Allah, so do not be wasteful.\nrefl\nوَقَالُواْ مَا فِي بُطُونِ هَٰذِهِ ٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمِ خَالِصَةٞ لِّذُكُورِنَا وَمُحَرَّمٌ عَلَىٰٓ أَزۡوَٰجِنَاۖ وَإِن يَكُن مَّيۡتَةٗ فَهُمۡ فِيهِ شُرَكَآءُۚ سَيَجۡزِيهِمۡ وَصۡفَهُمۡۚ إِنَّهُۥ حَكِيمٌ عَلِيمٞ ١٣٩\n(He is All-Wise, All-Knowing), this is the reasoning of Allah's promise to recompense them for their fabrication. The All-Wise, All-Knowing of what they did will not let them go unpunished since that is ordained by His wisdom. Al-Alusi: 8/389.\nThe verse concludes with the attributes of wisdom and knowledge. Why?\nوَقَالُواْ مَا فِي بُطُونِ هَٰذِهِ ٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمِ خَالِصَةٞ لِّذُكُورِنَا وَمُحَرَّمٌ عَلَىٰٓ أَزۡوَٰجِنَاۖ وَإِن يَكُن مَّيۡتَةٗ فَهُمۡ فِيهِ شُرَكَآءُۚ سَيَجۡزِيهِمۡ وَصۡفَهُمۡۚ إِنَّهُۥ حَكِيمٌ عَلِيمٞ ١٣٩\nThis verse proves that a scholar should learn the opposing argument to his views, even if he does not subscribe to it, so that he can identify its fallacy and be able to respond to it. That is why Allah informed His Messenger (ﷺ) and his Companions about the arguments of those who opposed them in their lifetime so that they would know the fallacies of their arguments. Al-Qurtubi: 9/48.\nWhat is the useful lesson that a student of Islamic studies can learn from this verse.\nوَقَالُواْ مَا فِي بُطُونِ هَٰذِهِ ٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمِ خَالِصَةٞ لِّذُكُورِنَا وَمُحَرَّمٌ عَلَىٰٓ أَزۡوَٰجِنَاۖ وَإِن يَكُن مَّيۡتَةٗ فَهُمۡ فِيهِ شُرَكَآءُۚ سَيَجۡزِيهِمۡ وَصۡفَهُمۡۚ إِنَّهُۥ حَكِيمٌ عَلِيمٞ ١٣٩\nOne of their foolish notions was that they would make what in the wombs of certain livestock - which they specified - prohibited to females but not to males, so they said, (What is in the bellies of these livestock is exclusively for our males) which means it is permissible for them, and women have no share in it (And is forbidden to our females) our womenfolk. This would apply if the offspring was born alive, but if it was stillborn, then they all had a share of it - in other words, it was permissible for both males and females. Al-Saadi: 276.\nIn this verse, there is a comparison between man-made laws and Sharia laws. Explain.\nقَدۡ خَسِرَ ٱلَّذِينَ قَتَلُوٓاْ أَوۡلَٰدَهُمۡ سَفَهَۢا بِغَيۡرِ عِلۡمٖ وَحَرَّمُواْ مَا رَزَقَهُمُ ٱللَّهُ ٱفۡتِرَآءً عَلَى ٱللَّهِۚ قَدۡ ضَلُّواْ وَمَا كَانُواْ مُهۡتَدِينَ ١٤٠\nThe Holy Quran often uses the word (loss) to describe the actions of those who seek to please Allah and achieve His reward, but they fell under His wrath and punishment because they exerted themselves [in doing the wrong things] and therefore, found the opposite of what they strived for. Ibn Ashur: 8/113.\nThe verse mentions the true loss. What is it?\nوَءَاتُواْ حَقَّهُۥ يَوۡمَ حَصَادِهِۦۖ\nAllah commands them to give its due zakah on the day of harvest because that is the time when the poor would expect it, and at that time it is easy for the growers to give it. Thus, the one who gives it will be known, and will stand out from the one who does not. Al-Saadi: 276.\nAllah commands them to give its due zakat on the day of harvest. Why?\nوَلَا تُسۡرِفُوٓاْۚ إِنَّهُۥ لَا يُحِبُّ ٱلۡمُسۡرِفِينَ ١٤١\nAz-Zuhri (a prominent scholar) said: \"Meaning: Do not spend your wealth to disobey Allah.\" Similar meaning was reported from Mujahid who said: \"If one spends as much as Abi Qabees (a mountain in Makkah) in gold for the cause of Allah, he will not be considered wasteful, but if he spends a single Dirham in disobeying Allah, then he is wasteful.\" Al-Alusi: 8/392.\nThe righteous predecessors explained the forbidden wastefulness. What is it?\nوَلَا تُسۡرِفُوٓاْۚ إِنَّهُۥ لَا يُحِبُّ ٱلۡمُسۡرِفِينَ ١٤١\nMeaning: Do not be wasteful in eating because this spoils the mind and the body. Allah says in another verse: (And eat and drink, but do not waste, for He does not like the wasteful) [7:31]. In his Sahih, Al-Bukhari recorded a Hadith without a chain of narration: (Eat, drink and clothe yourselves without extravagance or arrogance). Ibn Kathir: 2/174.\nWhy are we forbidden from being wasteful in eating?\nwords\nحِجرٌForbidden\nمَعرُوشَاتٍClimbing plants such as grapes\nوَغَيرَ مَعرُوشَاتٍPlants with trunks such as palm trees\nحَمُولَةًAnimals that are fit for labor and carrying loads, such as camels\nوَفَرشًاAnimals that are small and not fit for labor, such as sheep"],[147,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nList the types of prohibited food items in this verse, and learn the wisdom behind their prohibition.\nShare a message in which you explain that Halal food is far more blessed than Haram, thus we should suffice ourselves with what is permissible to eat.\nReview the types of food items that you consume, and avoid any items that are forbidden or doubtful to eat, as they can affect your faith and harm your body and mind.\nguid\nNo one is more unjust and wicked than one who fabricates lies against Allah and legislates for Allah's servants that which Allah did not.\nA scholar who delivers religious fatwas must have sufficient knowledge to do so, otherwise he risks being under the threat of this verse.\nThe respite given by Allah to violators does not indicate that they are free from punishment because no one knows but Allah when His wrath is coming.\nrefl\nأَمۡ كُنتُمۡ شُهَدَآءَ إِذۡ وَصَّىٰكُمُ ٱللَّهُ بِهَٰذَاۚ فَمَنۡ أَظۡلَمُ مِمَّنِ ٱفۡتَرَىٰ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ كَذِبٗا لِّيُضِلَّ ٱلنَّاسَ بِغَيۡرِ عِلۡمٍۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ١٤٤\n(Or were you present), have you witnessed that Allah has prohibited this? When they could not answer that, they started fabricating by saying: \"Allah ordained such and such!\" so, Allah says, (So, who does greater wrong than the one who fabricates lies against Allah in order to mislead people without knowledge). Allah exposed their lies since their saying had no proof. Al-Qurtubi: 9/79.\nWhat must one do before explaining a rule of Sharia on any matter?\nفَمَنۡ أَظۡلَمُ مِمَّنِ ٱفۡتَرَىٰ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ كَذِبٗا لِّيُضِلَّ ٱلنَّاسَ بِغَيۡرِ عِلۡمٍۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ١٤٤\nAllah Has unveiled their bad intention behind their fabrication. If one fabricates a lie against Allah for no reason, it would be considered a great wrongdoing. So, imagine how greater it would be if his intention is to mislead the people? Ibn Atiyah: 2/355.\nFabricating lies has different levels. Which one is the worst?\nفَمَنۡ أَظۡلَمُ مِمَّنِ ٱفۡتَرَىٰ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ كَذِبٗا لِّيُضِلَّ ٱلنَّاسَ بِغَيۡرِ عِلۡمٍۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ١٤٤\nIt is considered a wrongdoing for one to give a fatwa on a religious matter unless he believes -to a great degree- that its accurate and pleasing to Allah. That is because if he is among people who are competent for independent reasoning (Ijtihad), then he would rely on a valid proof; or if he is a follower of a competent scholar, then he must be sure that he conveys the right fatwa of his scholar. Ibn Ashur: 8/135.\nIt is forbidden to give fatwa without knowledge. Explain.\nأَوۡ دَمٗا مَّسۡفُوحًا\nThis refers to the blood which comes out of the animal at the time of slaughter, for it is the blood that would be harmful if it was retained in the body; when this blood is expelled from the body, the harm that may result from eating the meat is prevented. Al-Saadi: 277.\nAllah commands that the blood is expelled from the animal during slaughter. Why?\nأَوۡ دَمٗا مَّسۡفُوحًا\nWhat this phrase implies is that the blood that remains in the flesh and veins after slaughter is permissible and pure. Al-Saadi: 277.\nThe rule on running blood was clarified by Allah, what is the rule on the blood that remains in the flesh and veins?\nوَعَلَى ٱلَّذِينَ هَادُواْ حَرَّمۡنَا كُلَّ ذِي ظُفُرٖۖ وَمِنَ ٱلۡبَقَرِ وَٱلۡغَنَمِ حَرَّمۡنَا عَلَيۡهِمۡ شُحُومَهُمَآ إِلَّا مَا حَمَلَتۡ ظُهُورُهُمَآ أَوِ ٱلۡحَوَايَآ أَوۡ مَا ٱخۡتَلَطَ بِعَظۡمٖۚ ذَٰلِكَ جَزَيۡنَٰهُم بِبَغۡيِهِمۡۖ وَإِنَّا لَصَٰدِقُونَ ١٤٦\nThis prohibition was a punishment for (their transgression), which was killing their Prophets, averting people from the way of Allah, taking of usury, and consuming of the people's wealth unjustly. Al-Baghawi: 2/75.\nSins have ill effects. Explain in the light of this verse.\nوَعَلَى ٱلَّذِينَ هَادُواْ حَرَّمۡنَا كُلَّ ذِي ظُفُرٖۖ وَمِنَ ٱلۡبَقَرِ وَٱلۡغَنَمِ حَرَّمۡنَا عَلَيۡهِمۡ شُحُومَهُمَآ إِلَّا مَا حَمَلَتۡ ظُهُورُهُمَآ أَوِ ٱلۡحَوَايَآ أَوۡ مَا ٱخۡتَلَطَ بِعَظۡمٖۚ ذَٰلِكَ جَزَيۡنَٰهُم بِبَغۡيِهِمۡۖ وَإِنَّا لَصَٰدِقُونَ ١٤٦\n(And to the Jews) only the Jews. (For their transgression), due to the of killing their Prophets, taking of usury while they had been forbidden from it, and consuming of the people's wealth unjustly. Every time they committed a sin, they were punished by making unlawful what was lawful to them. Al-Alusi: 8/405.\nCausing harm to righteous people and killing them warrants divine punishments. Explain\nwords\nأَزوَاجٍPairs\nأُهِلَّ لِغَيرِ اللَّهِSacrifice offered in the name of other than Allah\nكُلَّ ذِي ظُفُرٍEvery animal of undivided hooves such as camels and ostriches\nالحَوَايَاIntestines"],[148,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nIdentify media platforms that are run by hypocrites and block them, as they spread nothing but lies and deception.\nPerform a good deed for your parents, today, whether they are alive or not, as Allah commands you to honor them.\nRead up on the interpretations of the commandments within this verse so that you are able to perform them.\nguid\nDo not grieve if you see a wrongdoer persisting in his sin, as Allah will bring down his wrath upon the wicked people and none can avert his punishment from them.\nFor one who calls others to Allah, he should not rule out the possibility that some will deny him, so he should not let that hinder his efforts.\nGuidance is in the hand of Allah, so ask Him for it.\nrefl\nفَإِن كَذَّبُوكَ فَقُل رَّبُّكُمۡ ذُو رَحۡمَةٖ وَٰسِعَةٖ\nThis is an encouragement to them to seek Allah's vast mercy and follow His Messenger (ﷺ). Ibn Kathir: 2/177.\nAllah's vast mercy is mentioned right after their rejection of His Messenger (ﷺ). Why?\nسَيَقُولُ ٱلَّذِينَ أَشۡرَكُواْ لَوۡ شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ مَآ أَشۡرَكۡنَا وَلَآ ءَابَآؤُنَا وَلَا حَرَّمۡنَا مِن شَيۡءٖۚ\nThe polytheists inferred from Allah's Will the negation of command and prohibition, what is reprehensible and what is praiseworthy and obedience and disobedience. Hence, whoever went along this way would definitely be a disbeliever. Ibn Taimyah: 3/112.\nIn light of this verse, clarify the risk of inferring from Allah's Will the negation of command and prohibition?\nقُلۡ تَعَالَوۡاْ أَتۡلُ مَا حَرَّمَ رَبُّكُمۡ عَلَيۡكُمۡۖ أَلَّا تُشۡرِكُواْ بِهِۦ شَيۡـٔٗاۖ وَبِٱلۡوَٰلِدَيۡنِ إِحۡسَٰنٗاۖ\nIn this verse, Allah mentions the major forbidden acts that are affirmed unanimously by every Sharia before Islam, and they were never abrogated by any religion. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \"These words are the same as what was revealed to Moses (peace be upon him).\" Ibn Juzay: 1/291.\nThese commandments have a certain distinction. What is it?\nقُلۡ تَعَالَوۡاْ أَتۡلُ مَا حَرَّمَ رَبُّكُمۡ عَلَيۡكُمۡۖ أَلَّا تُشۡرِكُواْ بِهِۦ شَيۡـٔٗاۖ وَبِٱلۡوَٰلِدَيۡنِ إِحۡسَٰنٗاۖ\nThis verse is a command from Allah to His Messenger (ﷺ) to call on all the people to listen to the reciting of what Allah prohibits. Therefore; it is the duty of scholars to convey this to the people and explain to them what is lawful and what is not. Al-Qurtubi: 9/106.\nIn this verse, what does Allah call on us to do?\nوَلَا تَقۡتُلُوٓاْ أَوۡلَٰدَكُم مِّنۡ إِمۡلَٰقٖ نَّحۡنُ نَرۡزُقُكُمۡ وَإِيَّاهُمۡۖ\nIn Surat Al-Isra', Allah says, (And do not kill your children for fear of poverty) [17:31]. Meaning: Do not kill your children for fear that you might become poor in the future. This is why Allah says, (We shall provide for them and for you) [17:31]. Thus mentioning the provision of the children first, which means do not fear poverty because of feeding your children. Certainly, their provision is provided by Allah. That is why Allah says, (We provide for you and for them) by starting with parents because they are already poor, and it is the appropriate subject here. Ibn Kathir: 2/180.\nThe mention of provision of parents in this Surah precedes that of their children, yet in Surat Al-Isra' it is the opposite. Why?\nوَلَا تَقۡرَبُواْ ٱلۡفَوَٰحِشَ مَا ظَهَرَ مِنۡهَا وَمَا بَطَنَۖ\nThis refers to actions that are visible and those that have to do with thoughts and intentions. The prohibition on approaching shameful deeds is more effective than a prohibition on merely doing them, because it includes a prohibition on their precursors and the means that lead to them. Al-Saadi: 280.\nNot only shameful sins are forbidden, but also approaching them. Why?\nوَلَا تَقۡرَبُواْ ٱلۡفَوَٰحِشَ مَا ظَهَرَ مِنۡهَا وَمَا بَطَنَۖ وَلَا تَقۡتُلُواْ ٱلنَّفۡسَ ٱلَّتِي حَرَّمَ ٱللَّهُ إِلَّا بِٱلۡحَقِّۚ\nThis part of the verse emphasizes this prohibition in specific, although it is included in the immoral sins committed openly and in secret. In Sahih Al-Bukhari and Sahih Muslim, it is recorded that Ibn Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"The blood of a Muslim who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am Allah's Messenger may not lawfully be shed but for one of three reasons: A life for a life, a married man who commits fornication, and one who renounces his religion and abandons the community.\" Ibn Kathir: 2/180.\nKilling a soul is included in the immoral sins. Why is it repeated?\nwords\nبَأسُهُHis punishment\nتَخرُصُونَYou are lying\nهَلُمَّBring forward\nيَعدِلُونَThey set up equals [with Allah]\nإِملاَقٍPoverty"],[149,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nSponsor an orphan or support one through a trusted organization, as Allah commands us to protect the wealth of orphans. The reward will even be greater when one spends his own money on an orphan.\nAdvise some defrauding sellers not to cheat people.\nTake a pledge to speak justly in every situation even if it is against yourself.\nguid\nAbiding by Islam and abjuring other religions and innovative teachings is the straight path to Paradise.\nAllah warns against meddling with orphans' rights and exploiting their wealth. Thus, keep far away from it.\nAnyone who owns a business that is based on measures and weights must fear Allah and be wary of defrauding people.\nrefl\nوَلَا تَقۡرَبُواْ مَالَ ٱلۡيَتِيمِ إِلَّا بِٱلَّتِي هِيَ أَحۡسَنُ حَتَّىٰ يَبۡلُغَ أَشُدَّهُۥۚ\nMeaning: Improving the orphan's property is achieved by preserving its capital and investing its incidentals. Al-Qurtubi: 9/111.\nHow can the orphan's property be improved?\nوَلَا تَقۡرَبُواْ مَالَ ٱلۡيَتِيمِ إِلَّا بِٱلَّتِي هِيَ أَحۡسَنُ حَتَّىٰ يَبۡلُغَ أَشُدَّهُۥۚ\nProtecting the orphan's right by preserving his property is specified in this verse to avert the likelihood of squandering the defenseless orphan's property by his guardian. Ibn Ashur: 8/164.\nThe verse specifies that protection the orphan's right is by preserving his property. Why?\nوَأَوۡفُواْ ٱلۡكَيۡلَ وَٱلۡمِيزَانَ بِٱلۡقِسۡطِۖ لَا نُكَلِّفُ نَفۡسًا إِلَّا وُسۡعَهَاۖ\nMeaning: As much as the soul is able to bear and without hardship. Hence, if anyone strives hard to be honest in terms of measures and weights then falls short without realizing, and without being negligent, then Allah is Pardoning and Forgiving. Al-Saadi: 280.\nThe command to give full measure and weight with justice is followed by stating that no soul is burdened beyond what it can bear. Why?\nوَأَنَّ هَٰذَا صِرَٰطِي مُسۡتَقِيمٗا فَٱتَّبِعُوهُۖ وَلَا تَتَّبِعُواْ ٱلسُّبُلَ فَتَفَرَّقَ بِكُمۡ عَن سَبِيلِهِۦۚ ذَٰلِكُمۡ وَصَّىٰكُم بِهِۦ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَتَّقُونَ ١٥٣\nThe other misguided ways include: Judaism, Christianity, Magians, and other deviant sects who follow their whims and innovate new ways in religion. Moreover, those who are deeply involved in argumentative philosophy are prone to deviation that lead to heresy. Al-Qurtubi: 9/117.\nAllah warns us against following certain ways. What are they?\nوَأَنَّ هَٰذَا صِرَٰطِي مُسۡتَقِيمٗا فَٱتَّبِعُوهُۖ وَلَا تَتَّبِعُواْ ٱلسُّبُلَ فَتَفَرَّقَ بِكُمۡ عَن سَبِيلِهِۦۚ ذَٰلِكُمۡ وَصَّىٰكُم بِهِۦ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَتَّقُونَ ١٥٣\n(And do not follow other ways), do not follow the different ways of religion such as Judaism, Christianity, and other false religions. This, also, includes: Innovators in religion who follow their misguided whims. The Prophet (ﷺ) drew a line then said: \"This is Allah's path.\" Thereafter he drew several lines on his right and left and said: \"These are paths on each of which there is a devil who invites people to follow it.\" Ibn Juzay: 1/292.\nSome people follow groups who have views contrary to that of Ahl Al-Sunnah while under the pretense that there is some good in it. What do you think about that?\nوَأَنَّ هَٰذَا صِرَٰطِي مُسۡتَقِيمٗا فَٱتَّبِعُوهُۖ وَلَا تَتَّبِعُواْ ٱلسُّبُلَ فَتَفَرَّقَ بِكُمۡ عَن سَبِيلِهِۦۚ\nAllah describes his path in the singular form because truth is one, but He describes other paths in the plural form because they are many and are divided. Ibn Kathir: 2/182.\nAllah's Path is stated in the singular form while other paths are in the plural form. Why?\nوَهَٰذَا كِتَٰبٌ أَنزَلۡنَٰهُ مُبَارَكٞ\nThe Holy Quran contains much good and abundant knowledge, and all other branches of knowledge are taken from it and all blessings are derived from it. There is nothing good but the Quran calls to it and encourages it. It mentions wisdom and interests that encourage one to pursue good. There is nothing evil but it forbids and warns against it, and it mentions reasons that put one off doing such things, and the bad consequences thereof. Al-Saadi: 281.\nThe Holy Quran contains many blessings. What are they?\nwords\nيَبلُغَ أَشُدَّهُAttains maturity\nبِالقِسطِWith justice\nدِرَاسَتِهِمStudying their books\nوَصَدَفَTurns away"],[150,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nAdvise some grave worshipers that based on this verse, only Allah is worthy of worship.\nAsk Allah for sincerity in all of your matters, and never do anything without having a sincere intention.\nDo good to a poor person.\nguid\nDo not delay repentance and doing good deeds, for a time may come when you cannot do them.\nDefy polytheists and offer your rites of sacrifice only to Allah alone.\nOne who calls others to Allah should diversify his ways of preaching to others. For instance, using intimidation to discourage people from committing sins by mentioning Allah's torment and punishment, and using exhortation to invite them to His mercy by mentioning Allah's blessings and pleasure, or using a mix of both approaches.\nrefl\nيَوۡمَ يَأۡتِي بَعۡضُ ءَايَٰتِ رَبِّكَ لَا يَنفَعُ نَفۡسًا إِيمَٰنُهَا لَمۡ تَكُنۡ ءَامَنَتۡ مِن قَبۡلُ أَوۡ كَسَبَتۡ فِيٓ إِيمَٰنِهَا خَيۡرٗاۗ قُلِ ٱنتَظِرُوٓاْ إِنَّا مُنتَظِرُونَ ١٥٨\nScholars said: A soul will not benefit from its faith when the Sun rises from the West because fear will be overwhelming so that all of its desires will subside and all of its strengths will diminish. All people will be certain of the end of this life, and therefore, they become like one who is facing his own death and tries to repent, but it will be too late. Al-Qurtubi: 9/130.\nA soul will not benefit from its faith when the Sun rises from the West. Why?\nيَوۡمَ يَأۡتِي بَعۡضُ ءَايَٰتِ رَبِّكَ لَا يَنفَعُ نَفۡسًا إِيمَٰنُهَا لَمۡ تَكُنۡ ءَامَنَتۡ مِن قَبۡلُ أَوۡ كَسَبَتۡ فِيٓ إِيمَٰنِهَا خَيۡرٗاۗ\nThe wisdom behind that is obvious. Faith is only of benefit if it is faith in the unseen and is voluntary on the part of the individual. Once the signs appear, then it becomes a matter of faith in the seen and so faith will no longer be of benefit because it is more akin to faith when one has no other choice, like the faith of one who is drowning or burning to death and the like, who when they see death, give up what they were doing. Al-Saadi: 281.\nIn the light of this verse, describe, in brief, the importance of believing in the unseen?\nأَوۡ كَسَبَتۡ فِيٓ إِيمَٰنِهَا خَيۡرٗاۗ\nMan may attain good by means of his faith; acts of obedience, righteousness and piety are only of benefit and can only develop if the individual has faith. If his heart is devoid of faith, then, none of these deeds will be of any benefit to him. Al-Saadi: 282.\nSome disbelievers may do some good deeds in this life. Does that benefit them in the Hereafter? Why?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ فَرَّقُواْ دِينَهُمۡ وَكَانُواْ شِيَعٗا لَّسۡتَ مِنۡهُمۡ فِي شَيۡءٍۚ\n(Those who have made divisions in their religion and turned into sects) Mujahid said: \"Those are the people of religious innovations and doubts in their minds.\" Ibn Taimyah: 3/117.\nAre the people of religious innovations included in this verse?\nقُلۡ إِنَّنِي هَدَىٰنِي رَبِّيٓ إِلَىٰ صِرَٰطٖ مُّسۡتَقِيمٖ دِينٗا قِيَمٗا مِّلَّةَ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ حَنِيفٗاۚ وَمَا كَانَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ ١٦١ قُلۡ إِنَّ صَلَاتِي وَنُسُكِي وَمَحۡيَايَ وَمَمَاتِي لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ١٦٢\nThe correct religion is a general term; then Allah singles out for mention the noblest acts of worship, as He says, (Say, \"Indeed, my prayer, my rites of sacrifice) - this is because of the virtue of these two acts of worship and what they imply of loving Allah, devoting worship sincerely to Him alone and drawing closer to Him in one's heart and by means of one's words and actions. Sacrifice means giving up what one loves of wealth or property for what is dearer to him, namely Allah. Al-Saadi: 282.\nPrayer and sacrifice are included in the first verse. Why are they singled out for mention?\nقُلۡ إِنَّ صَلَاتِي وَنُسُكِي وَمَحۡيَايَ وَمَمَاتِي لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ١٦٢\nMeaning: My life and my death (are for Allah): He gives me life and He takes it away. It also said that my life is spent in doing good deeds for Allah, and when my death comes I will die as a believer in Allah, the Lord of the worlds. Al-Baghawi: 2/86.\nHow can living and dying be for Allah, Lord of the worlds?\nإِنَّ رَبَّكَ سَرِيعُ ٱلۡعِقَابِ وَإِنَّهُۥ لَغَفُورٞ رَّحِيمُۢ ١٦٥\nThis is both exhortation and intimidation, by reminding the believers that Allah is Swift in reckoning and punishment with those who disobey Him and defy His Messengers, and He is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful for those who take Him as protector and follow His Messengers in the narrations and commandments they conveyed. Sometimes, Allah calls His servants to them with exhortation, describing Paradise and making them eager for what He has for them. Other times, He calls them with intimidation, mentioning Hellfire and its torment and punishment, as well as, the Day of Resurrection and its horrors. At times, Allah mentions both. Ibn Kathir: 2/191.\nCalling others to Allah can be by exhortation or intimidation or both. Why?\nwords\nشِيَعًاSects\nقِيَمًاUpright\nوَنُسُكِيMy rites of sacrifice\nوَلاَ تَزِرُWill not bear\nوَازِرَةٌA bearer of sin\nوِزرَA sin"],[151,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, guard me from what is in front of me and behind me, from my right, and from my left, and from above me. I seek refuge in Your Greatness from being struck down from beneath me.\"\nMention the Name of Allah always, especially when people are heedless.\nConfess to your wrongdoing and sin today before Allah, make up for it and repent from it, as when Allah's punishment comes, repenting would be of no benefit to you.\nguid\nConstant recital of the Quran and reflecting on its meanings is a means to remind yourself to do good deeds, and reform your inward and outward.\nFollowing the revelations from Allah is an obligation, and following the ways of religious innovators is prohibited.\nLearning lessons from the destruction of corrupt and sinful nations is imperative.\nrefl\nالٓمٓصٓ ١ كِتَٰبٌ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡكَ فَلَا يَكُن فِي صَدۡرِكَ حَرَجٞ مِّنۡهُ لِتُنذِرَ بِهِۦ وَذِكۡرَىٰ لِلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٢\nThese disjointed letters of the Arabic alphabet at the beginning of some Surahs in the Quran are followed by mentioning the Quran, the revelation or something similar in meaning, which indicates that the aim of starting with these spelled letters is a challenge to the Arabs to show their incapability of producing the like of this Quran, [even though it is made up of letters from the Arabic alphabet]. Ibn Ashur: 8/10.\nThe disjointed letters are often followed by mentioning the Quran. Why?\nٱتَّبِعُواْ مَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡكُم مِّن رَّبِّكُمۡ وَلَا تَتَّبِعُواْ مِن دُونِهِۦٓ أَوۡلِيَآءَۗ قَلِيلٗا مَّا تَذَكَّرُونَ ٣\nThis verse proves that where there is a clear text in the revelation, then one must disregard opinions. Al-Qurtubi: 9/151.\nWhat is the guidance of Quran for one who disregards a clear proof and follows thoughts and views?\nوَكَم مِّن قَرۡيَةٍ أَهۡلَكۡنَٰهَا فَجَآءَهَا بَأۡسُنَا بَيَٰتًا أَوۡهُمۡ قَآئِلُونَ ٤\nIt means that Allah's command, torment and vengeance came over them at night or while taking a nap in the middle of the day. Both of these times are periods of rest and leisure or heedlessness and amusement. Ibn Kathir: 2/192.\nNight and noon are singled out for the occurrence of Allah’s Punishment. Why?\nفَمَا كَانَ دَعۡوَىٰهُمۡ إِذۡ جَآءَهُم بَأۡسُنَآ إِلَّآ أَن قَالُوٓاْ إِنَّا كُنَّا ظَٰلِمِينَ ٥\nTheir rejection of the message is a transgression because it is a rejection of clear proofs and hence it is a transgression. Ibn Ashur: 8/32.\nRejection of clear proofs is a transgression. Explain.\nفَلَنَسۡـَٔلَنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ أُرۡسِلَ إِلَيۡهِمۡ وَلَنَسۡـَٔلَنَّ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلِينَ ٦\nThere is a consensus among scholars of Ahl Al-Sunnah that the words of any person are subject to acceptance or rejection except that which are of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ), for he must be believed in everything he narrated, and obeyed in everything he enjoined. The Messenger (ﷺ) is Infallible who does not speak out of his own desire but it is a revelation sent down to him. Moreover, on the Day of Resurrection, people will be questioned about him, as Allah says, (Then We will surely question those to whom [a message] was sent, and We will surely question the messengers). Ibn Taimyah: 3/137.\nA remedy for religious fanaticism is to know that the words of anyone can be accepted or rejected except that which are of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ). Explain.\nوَٱلۡوَزۡنُ يَوۡمَئِذٍ ٱلۡحَقُّۚ فَمَن ثَقُلَتۡ مَوَٰزِينُهُۥ فَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡمُفۡلِحُونَ ٨\nIf you say, \"Does Allah not already know the weights of people's deeds? So, what is the wisdom behind weighing them?\" I say, \"There are many wisdoms in weighing the deeds such as displaying justice and the fact that Allah does not wrong people in the least, and revealing to people all of their good deeds and bad ones.\" Al-Qasimi: 1/297.\nWhat is the wisdom behind weighing people's deeds on the Day of Resurrection, even though Allah is already aware of them?\nوَلَقَدۡ خَلَقۡنَٰكُمۡ ثُمَّ صَوَّرۡنَٰكُمۡ ثُمَّ قُلۡنَا لِلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةِ ٱسۡجُدُواْ لِأٓدَمَ فَسَجَدُوٓاْ إِلَّآ إِبۡلِيسَ لَمۡ يَكُن مِّنَ ٱلسَّٰجِدِينَ ١١\nAllah informs the Children of Adam about the honor of their father and the enmity of satan, who still has envy for them and for their father Adam (peace be upon him), so they should beware of him and not follow in his footsteps. Ibn Kathir: 2/193.\nWhat lesson can a Muslim learn from satan's refusal to prostrate to his father (Adam)?\nwords\nبَأسُنَاOur Punishment\nبَيَاتًاSleeping at night\nقَائِلُونَResting at noon\nوَالوَزنُThe weighing of people’s deeds\nمَعَايِشَMeans of livelihood"],[152,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nDo a good deed today that reflects humbleness to others.\nThink of traits and blessings that Allah has bestowed upon you, and be grateful to Him.\nSeek refuge with Allah from the accursed satan repeatedly today, and say, \"O Allah, guard me from what is in front of me and behind me, from my right, and from my left, and from above me. I seek refuge in Your Greatness from being struck down from beneath me.\"\nguid\nThe narrative of Adam (u) with Iblis affirms that this enemy has prepared very well to entrap you, so you must be prepared to fend off his deceptions.\nIblis' only weapon against children of Adam is whispering and making sins alluring to them.\nNot everyone who gives advice and swears by Allah is truthful. The past history of a person reveals the truth about him.\nrefl\nقَالَ مَا مَنَعَكَ أَلَّا تَسۡجُدَ إِذۡ أَمَرۡتُكَۖ قَالَ أَنَا۠ خَيۡرٞ مِّنۡهُ خَلَقۡتَنِي مِن نَّارٖ وَخَلَقۡتَهُۥ مِن طِينٖ ١٢\n(He said, \"I am better than him), this was how Iblis reasoned his refusal to prostrate to Adam (peace be upon him). Iblis' objection to Allah's command by alleging that being superior to Adam (peace be upon him), then he should not be commanded to prostrate to him. This was a refusal to submit to Allah's command, which constituted disbelief, however it is not disbelief out of denial of Allah. Ibn Juzay: 1/297.\nA creature's arrogance entices him, sometimes, to refuse to submit to the commands of Allah by allegedly using reasoning, thus he becomes a disbeliever. Explain in light of this verse.\nقَالَ مَا مَنَعَكَ أَلَّا تَسۡجُدَ إِذۡ أَمَرۡتُكَۖ قَالَ أَنَا۠ خَيۡرٞ مِّنۡهُ خَلَقۡتَنِي مِن نَّارٖ وَخَلَقۡتَهُۥ مِن طِينٖ ١٢\nThis argument of Iblis, (\"I am better than him; You created me from fire and created him from clay\"), was false because he refused to submit to a clear command from Allah by using analogical deduction. Ibn Taimyah: 3/138.\nWhy was Iblis' argument false?\nخَلَقۡتَنِي مِن نَّارٖ وَخَلَقۡتَهُۥ مِن طِينٖ ١٢\nIblis lied by regarding the substance of fire as being superior to the substance of clay or mud, for clay has the characteristics of humility, tranquility and dignity, and from it emerge the blessings of the earth, such as trees and all kinds of plants. As for fire, it has the characteristics of fickleness and capriciousness, and it burns. Al-Saadi: 284.\nIblis was mistaken in regarding the substance of fire as being superior to the substance of clay. Why?\nقَالَ فَٱهۡبِطۡ مِنۡهَا فَمَا يَكُونُ لَكَ أَن تَتَكَبَّرَ فِيهَا فَٱخۡرُجۡ إِنَّكَ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰغِرِينَ ١٣\n(For it is not for you to be arrogant therein), this is because Paradise's inhabitants are the humble angels. (So get out; indeed, you are of the debased) of the humiliated. This proves that whoever disobeys Allah becomes humiliated. Al-Qurtubi: 9/169.\nWhat are the traits of those who are close to Allah? What are the traits of those who are faraway from Him?\nفَٱخۡرُجۡ إِنَّكَ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰغِرِينَ ١٣\n(So get out; indeed, you are of the debased), of the humiliated and disgraced as a just recompense for his ill intentions, by giving him the opposite of what he intended. Ibn Kathir: 2/195.\nIblis was punished by humiliation and disgrace. Why?\nثُمَّ لَأٓتِيَنَّهُم مِّنۢ بَيۡنِ أَيۡدِيهِمۡ وَمِنۡ خَلۡفِهِمۡ وَعَنۡ أَيۡمَٰنِهِمۡ وَعَن شَمَآئِلِهِمۡۖ وَلَا تَجِدُ أَكۡثَرَهُمۡ شَٰكِرِينَ ١٧\n(Then I will come against them from their front and from their back, from their right and from their left, and You will not find most of them grateful), Ibn Abbas (t) and Ikrimah said about this verse: Iblis did not say \"from above them\" because he knew that Allah is above them. Ibn Taimyah: 3/140.\nIblis did not mention \"from above them.\" Why?\nفَوَسۡوَسَ لَهُمَا ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ لِيُبۡدِيَ لَهُمَا مَا وُۥرِيَ عَنۡهُمَا مِن سَوۡءَٰتِهِمَا\n(Of their private parts), in the original Arabic text, the word used for private parts is (saw'ah), which is derived from a root word that means \"shame\" in Arabic to indicate that exposing one's private parts is a shameful act. Al-Qurtubi: 9/175.\nIn the original text, the word (saw’ah) is used for private parts. Why?\nwords\nالصَّاغِرِينَThose who are humiliated and disgraced\nمَذؤومًاReproached and disgraced\nمَدحُورًاExpelled\nوَطَفِقَاThey began\nيَخصِفَانِThey put together [leaves of the Garden]"],[153,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nThink of a sin that you had committed, repent today, and ask for forgiveness as much as seventy times.\nSay this great supplication today, during times that is likely to be answered, as it is a supplication of those who are the nearest ones to Allah.\nMaintain obligatory prayers at the mosque.\nguid\nWhoever wronged himself is a loser unless he is saved by his Lord's mercy and forgiveness.\nThe dire consequence of sin was the cause for expelling Iblis from Allah's mercy, and the removing of Adam (peace be upon him) from the Garden, so beware of committing sins.\nBeware of satan, and do not be heedless of his ways and tricks.\nrefl\nقَالَا رَبَّنَا ظَلَمۡنَآ أَنفُسَنَا وَإِن لَّمۡ تَغۡفِرۡ لَنَا وَتَرۡحَمۡنَا لَنَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلۡخَٰسِرِينَ ٢٣\nSome scholars said: \"Two servants, Adam (peace be upon him) and Iblis, each one committed a sin. Adam (peace be upon him) repented, and Allah accepted his repentance, chose and guided him. Iblis insisted and protested using the argument of fate and destiny. Whoever repents from his sin, will be like his father, Adam (peace be upon him), and whoever insists and uses the fate argument, will be like Iblis. Ibn Taimyah: 3/142\nIn light of this verse, show the importance of the quick admission of guilt and seeking forgiveness?\nقَالَا رَبَّنَا ظَلَمۡنَآ أَنفُسَنَا وَإِن لَّمۡ تَغۡفِرۡ لَنَا وَتَرۡحَمۡنَا لَنَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلۡخَٰسِرِينَ ٢٣\nForgiveness removes the sins, and mercy brings down blessings. Ibn Taimyah: 3/142.\nWhat is the difference between forgiveness and mercy in this verse?\nقَالَا رَبَّنَا ظَلَمۡنَآ أَنفُسَنَا وَإِن لَّمۡ تَغۡفِرۡ لَنَا وَتَرۡحَمۡنَا لَنَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلۡخَٰسِرِينَ ٢٣\nWhoever follows the example of Adam by admitting his guilt, asking for forgiveness, regretting it and giving it up -if he commits a sin- his Lord will draw him near and guide him. But whoever follows the example of Iblis by carrying on -if he commits a sin- and continuing to increase it, will only go further away from Allah. Al-Saadi: 285.\nIn the story of Adam (peace be upon him) and Iblis, there is a great lesson for one who commits a sin. What is it?\nوَلِبَاسُ ٱلتَّقۡوَىٰ ذَٰلِكَ خَيۡرٞۚ\nMeaning: It is better than physical clothing, for the garment of piety lasts and does not wear out or vanish; it is the beauty of the heart and soul. As for outward clothing, its purpose is to cover the \"awrah\" sometimes, or to be an adornment for the wearer, and it has no other benefit beyond that. Al-Saadi: 286.\nWhy is the clothing of piety better than physical clothing?\nإِنَّهُۥ يَرَىٰكُمۡ هُوَ وَقَبِيلُهُۥ مِنۡ حَيۡثُ لَا تَرَوۡنَهُمۡۗ\nMalik bin Dinar (a prominent scholar) said: \"An enemy who sees you while you cannot see him is indeed a formidable adversary, except to those who are protected by Allah.\" Al-Baghawi: 2/97.\nAn enemy who sees you while you cannot see him is very dangerous. Explain.\nإِنَّا جَعَلۡنَا ٱلشَّيَٰطِينَ أَوۡلِيَآءَ لِلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤۡمِنُونَ ٢٧\nMeaning: This is more of a punishment to them that Allah makes them equal in going astray. Al-Qurtubi: 9/393.\nWho are the devils' allies?\nإِنَّهُمُ ٱتَّخَذُواْ ٱلشَّيَٰطِينَ أَوۡلِيَآءَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ وَيَحۡسَبُونَ أَنَّهُم مُّهۡتَدُونَ ٣٠\nThis proves that guidance is by the grace and blessing of Allah, and that misguidance results from His forsaking a person if that person, because of his ignorance and wrongdoing, takes satan as an ally, thus becoming the cause of his own misguidance. The one who thinks that he is guided when in fact he is misguided has no excuse. Al-Saadi: 287.\nMost of the followers of deviant sects believe that they are guided to the truth. Does that benefit them?\nwords\nيُوَارِي سَوآتِكُمClothing to conceal your private parts\nوَرِيشًاAnd as adornment\nيَفتِنَنَّكُمُDeceives you\nبِالقِسطِJustice"],[154,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nIn keeping with this verse, dress nicely today when you go to pray.\nShare messages in which you warn others against the fundamental sins mentioned in this verse.\nShare a message in which you warn others against giving fatwas or saying about Allah anything without proper and sufficient knowledge.\nguid\nDo not be wasteful when eating, drinking and spending, as Allah does not like the wasteful.\nDifferentiate between what you hate and what Allah Has made forbidden, as it is not allowed for anyone to prohibit something that is made permissible by Allah out of hatred.\nSocieties are like individuals; society perishes when a disease spreads to most people, just as an individual perishes when a disease takes over most of his body.\nrefl\nيَٰبَنِيٓ ءَادَمَ خُذُواْ زِينَتَكُمۡ عِندَ كُلِّ مَسۡجِدٖ وَكُلُواْ وَٱشۡرَبُواْ وَلَا تُسۡرِفُوٓاْۚ إِنَّهُۥ لَا يُحِبُّ ٱلۡمُسۡرِفِينَ ٣١\nIt is said that dressing well means wearing more than what is necessary to cover the body such as dressing with adornments like perfumes and tooth cleanser (Miswak) for Friday prayers. (Eat and drink, but do not waste, for He does not like the wasteful) means: do not consume more food than you need. Medical doctors said: \"This verse contains the best medical advice.\" Ibn Juzay: 1/300.\nThis verse combines what is best for the heart and body. Explain.\nقُلۡ مَنۡ حَرَّمَ زِينَةَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلَّتِيٓ أَخۡرَجَ لِعِبَادِهِۦ وَٱلطَّيِّبَٰتِ مِنَ ٱلرِّزۡقِۚ قُلۡ هِيَ لِلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا خَالِصَةٗ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِۗ كَذَٰلِكَ نُفَصِّلُ ٱلۡأٓيَٰتِ لِقَوۡمٖ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٣٢\nAllah Has bestowed this abundance of good things upon His servants to help them to worship Him, so He did not make it permissible to any but His believing servants. Hence He says, (Say, \"They are for the believers in the life of this world [although shared by others], and will be exclusively theirs on the Day of Resurrection]. What we may understand from the verse is that regarding the one who does not believe in Allah -rather he uses the blessings to commit sin- is that the blessings are not meant for him. Rather, he will be punished for having them and enjoying them, and he will be questioned about them on the Day of Resurrection. Al-Saadi: 287.\nWhat is the wisdom behind making the blessings lawful for the believers?\nقُلۡ مَنۡ حَرَّمَ زِينَةَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلَّتِيٓ أَخۡرَجَ لِعِبَادِهِۦ وَٱلطَّيِّبَٰتِ مِنَ ٱلرِّزۡقِۚ قُلۡ هِيَ لِلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا خَالِصَةٗ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِۗ كَذَٰلِكَ نُفَصِّلُ ٱلۡأٓيَٰتِ لِقَوۡمٖ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٣٢\nThis verse recommends dressing well with adornments for Eid and Friday prayers, when meeting people, and when visiting with the brethren. Al-Qurtubi: 9/203.\nIn light of this verse, explain this Prophetic Hadith: \"Allah is Beautiful and He likes beauty.\"?\nقُلۡ هِيَ لِلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا خَالِصَةٗ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِۗ\nIn this life, the adornments and lawful provisions are for the believers with some worries and bitterness; however, on the Day of Resurrection, they will be exclusively and worry-free for the believers. Al-Baghawi: 2/100.\nHow will the adornments and lawful provisions be exclusively for the believers on the Day of Resurrection?\nكَذَٰلِكَ نُفَصِّلُ ٱلۡأٓيَٰتِ لِقَوۡمٖ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٣٢ قُلۡ إِنَّمَا حَرَّمَ رَبِّيَ ٱلۡفَوَٰحِشَ مَا ظَهَرَ مِنۡهَا وَمَا بَطَنَ\n(Thus We explain the revelations in detail), We clarify them and make them clear (for people who have knowledge) because they are the ones who will benefit from what Allah explains in detail of His revelations; they know that they are from Allah, so they appreciate them and understand them. Then Allah mentions the things that He has prohibited, which are prohibited in all divinely revealed laws: (Say: My Lord has only forbidden shameful acts): that is, major sins which people find shameful and repugnant because they are so horrible, such as fornication, adultery, homosexuality and so on. Al-Saadi: 287.\nThe revelations are explained in details for people of knowledge. Why?\nقُلۡ إِنَّمَا حَرَّمَ رَبِّيَ ٱلۡفَوَٰحِشَ مَا ظَهَرَ مِنۡهَا وَمَا بَطَنَ وَٱلۡإِثۡمَ وَٱلۡبَغۡيَ بِغَيۡرِ ٱلۡحَقِّ وَأَن تُشۡرِكُواْ بِٱللَّهِ مَا لَمۡ يُنَزِّلۡ بِهِۦ سُلۡطَٰنٗا وَأَن تَقُولُواْ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ مَا لَا تَعۡلَمُونَ ٣٣\nThe major sins of which Allah says, (Say, \"My Lord has forbidden shameful acts done openly or in secret, sinfulness, unjustified aggression, associating partners with Allah for which He has not sent down any authority, and saying about Allah that of which you have no knowledge) are affirmed by the Sharias of all the Prophets. Ibn Taimyah: 3/157.\nIn light of this verse, what are the major sins?\nقُلۡ إِنَّمَا حَرَّمَ رَبِّيَ ٱلۡفَوَٰحِشَ مَا ظَهَرَ مِنۡهَا وَمَا بَطَنَ\nThe proper meanings of what is \"good\" and \"bad\" can only be derived from Sharia. Moreover, the meaning of (Shameful acts), which is mentioned here, indicates everything that is prohibited in other parts of Sharia. Hence, everything which is prohibited by Sharia is a shameful act even though it may not be opposed by some people's minds, such as men's wearing of silk and gold, etc. Ibn Atiyah: 2/395.\nWhat are the criteria of \"good\" and \"bad\" on which the lawful and unlawful are based?\nwords\nزِينَتَكُمDressed well with adornments\nنَصِيبُهُمTheir portion\nمِنَ الكِتَابِTheir destined punishment"],[155,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nShare a message in which you warn others about the habit of cursing, as it is one of the traits of the people of Hellfire.\nWhen you leave your home, say, \"I seek refuge with Allah lest I stray or be led astray, or slip or made to slip, or cause injustice, or suffer injustice, or do wrong, or behave foolishly, or be treated foolishly.\"\nRemind those around you of the importance of purity of the heart, as it is one of the traits of the people of Paradise.\nguid\nThe wicked and sinful friends will curse one another on the Day of Resurrection because they were the cause of each other's torment.\nThe wealth and status of a person will not benefit you if you follow his misguidance, rather he will disown you in the Hereafter.\nAbiding by Allah's Sharia is a feasible and easy task, so seek Allah's Help and do not be weakened.\nrefl\nقَالَ ٱدۡخُلُواْ فِيٓ أُمَمٖ قَدۡ خَلَتۡ مِن قَبۡلِكُم مِّنَ ٱلۡجِنِّ وَٱلۡإِنسِ فِي ٱلنَّارِۖ كُلَّمَا دَخَلَتۡ أُمَّةٞ لَّعَنَتۡ أُخۡتَهَاۖ حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا ٱدَّارَكُواْ فِيهَا جَمِيعٗا قَالَتۡ أُخۡرَىٰهُمۡ لِأُولَىٰهُمۡ رَبَّنَا هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ أَضَلُّونَا فَـَٔاتِهِمۡ عَذَابٗا ضِعۡفٗا مِّنَ ٱلنَّارِۖ قَالَ لِكُلّٖ ضِعۡفٞ وَلَٰكِن لَّا تَعۡلَمُونَ ٣٨\nThis dialogue between the leaders and their followers of past nations is narrated by Allah to warn Muslim leaders not to lead their followers to misguidance by allowing them to follow their own desires. Moreover, it warns the followers against indulgence in supporting leaders who encourage them to pursue their own desires, and do not exhort them to do the right thing. Ibn Ashur: 8/125.\nWhat is the benefit of narrating the dialogue between the leaders and their followers?\nقَالَ لِكُلّٖ ضِعۡفٞ وَلَٰكِن لَّا تَعۡلَمُونَ ٣٨\nEach group will not know what happens to the other, for if some of them know that the punishment to others exceeds theirs, it will give them some comfort. Al-Qurtubi: 9/222.\nThe level of punishment of the people in Hellfire is hidden from each other. Why?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَذَّبُواْ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا وَٱسۡتَكۡبَرُواْ عَنۡهَا لَا تُفَتَّحُ لَهُمۡ أَبۡوَٰبُ ٱلسَّمَآءِ وَلَا يَدۡخُلُونَ ٱلۡجَنَّةَ حَتَّىٰ يَلِجَ ٱلۡجَمَلُ فِي سَمِّ ٱلۡخِيَاطِۚ وَكَذَٰلِكَ نَجۡزِي ٱلۡمُجۡرِمِينَ ٤٠\nWhat is meant in this verse is that the gates of Heaven are opened for the souls of the believers who complied with the commands of Allah and believed in His revelations, so that they may ascend to Allah and reach wherever Allah wills they should reach of the higher realm. They will have the joy of being close to their Lord and of earning His good pleasure. Al-Saadi: 288.\nWhat is the benefit in knowing that the souls of disbelievers will not enter the gates of Heaven?\nلَهُم مِّن جَهَنَّمَ مِهَادٞ وَمِن فَوۡقِهِمۡ غَوَاشٖۚ وَكَذَٰلِكَ نَجۡزِي ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٤١\n(They will have from Hell a bed) as a mattress, (and over them coverings) as a bed cover; and therefore, they will be surrounded by fire from all sides. Al-Baghawi: 2/103.\nAs the forbidden worldly pleasures surround the body of the disbeliever, the punishment will also do the same on the Day of Judgment. Explain?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ لَا نُكَلِّفُ نَفۡسًا إِلَّا وُسۡعَهَآ\n(But those who believed and did righteous deeds) their hearts have believed and they performed good deeds with their limbs and senses, as compared to those who disbelieved in the verses of Allah and were arrogant toward them. Moreover, Allah said that embracing faith and implementing it are easy, (We charge no soul except [within] its capacity). Ibn Kathir: 2/205.\nRejecting faith and guidance is not due to their difficulty. Explain.\nوَنَزَعۡنَا مَا فِي صُدُورِهِم مِّنۡ غِلّٖ تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهِمُ ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُۖ\nAllah says that for those who will be in Paradise, He will remove from their hearts spite, resentment and animosity that they had toward each other when they were in this worldly life, so they will enter Paradise seated on thrones facing one another. They will not envy each other for that which Allah has granted some of them, and rivers will flow beneath them. Al-Tabari: 12/437.\nHappiness can be attained by avoiding feelings of envy and spite toward others. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَقَالُواْ ٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِي هَدَىٰنَا لِهَٰذَا وَمَا كُنَّا لِنَهۡتَدِيَ لَوۡلَآ أَنۡ هَدَىٰنَا ٱللَّهُۖ\nWhen one performs good deeds, his action itself is a favor and a blessing from Allah by way of guidance and faith, as people of Paradise will say, (All praise be to Allah Who has guided us to this, for We would not have been guided to this if Allah had not guided us). Ibn Taimyah: 3/162.\nDoing good deeds is a favor and a blessing from Allah. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nادَّارَكُواGathered inside\nيَلِجَPasses through\nسَمِّ الخِيَاطِThe eye of a needle\nغَوَاشٍCoverings [over them]"],[156,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nRead a book about the traits of the people of Paradise and those of Hellfire.\nProvide water to a thirsty person and make it a habit so that Allah will reward you in the Hereafter.\nDetermine which Islamic rulings you have not taken seriously and try to conform to them in a way that is pleasing to Allah.\nguid\nThe wrongdoers are known for attacking Islam by seeking to make it crooked, westernize society, destroy virtues, cast doubts on religion and glorify the disbelievers.\nYour wealth, followers, relatives and status will not benefit you in any way in the Hereafter, but only your good deeds will.\nNever disrespect a person for being poor and destitute.\nrefl\nوَنَادَىٰٓ أَصۡحَٰبُ ٱلۡجَنَّةِ أَصۡحَٰبَ ٱلنَّارِ أَن قَدۡ وَجَدۡنَا مَا وَعَدَنَا رَبُّنَا حَقّٗا فَهَلۡ وَجَدتُّم مَّا وَعَدَ رَبُّكُمۡ حَقّٗاۖ قَالُواْ نَعَمۡۚ فَأَذَّنَ مُؤَذِّنُۢ بَيۡنَهُمۡ أَن لَّعۡنَةُ ٱللَّهِ عَلَى ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٤٤\nThis call of the people of Paradise to the people of Hellfire is a censure and a rebuke to increase their anguish. Ibn Atiyah: 2/402.\nWhat is the benefit of the call of people of Paradise to the people of Hellfire?\nوَهُم بِٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ كَٰفِرُونَ ٤٥\nThis is what caused them to deviate from the straight path and to focus on their own unlawful whims and desires, and not to believe in the resurrection or fear the punishment or hope for reward. Al-Saadi: 290.\nWhat is the effect of belief in resurrection and the Hereafter?\nوَبَيۡنَهُمَا حِجَابٞۚ وَعَلَى ٱلۡأَعۡرَافِ رِجَالٞ يَعۡرِفُونَ كُلَّۢا بِسِيمَىٰهُمۡۚ وَنَادَوۡاْ أَصۡحَٰبَ ٱلۡجَنَّةِ أَن سَلَٰمٌ عَلَيۡكُمۡۚ لَمۡ يَدۡخُلُوهَا وَهُمۡ يَطۡمَعُونَ ٤٦\nBetween the people of Paradise and the people of Hellfire, there will be a barrier called Al-A'raf (the Heights), which is not part of Paradise nor of Hellfire, but it overlooks both, and it is possible to look down from it and see both groups. On top of this barrier will be men who will recognize both the people of Paradise and of Hellfire (by their marks) that is, signs in them from which they may be recognized and distinguished. When they look at the people of Paradise, they will call out to them, saying, (Peace be upon you). In other words, they will greet them even though -up to this point- they will not have entered Paradise, but they will hope to enter it, and Allah will not put hope in their hearts except for the reason that He will want to bestow honor upon them. Al-Saadi: 290.\nWho are the people of the Heights (Al-A'raf )?\nوَنَادَىٰٓ أَصۡحَٰبُ ٱلۡأَعۡرَافِ رِجَالٗا يَعۡرِفُونَهُم بِسِيمَىٰهُمۡ قَالُواْ مَآ أَغۡنَىٰ عَنكُمۡ جَمۡعُكُمۡ وَمَا كُنتُمۡ تَسۡتَكۡبِرُونَ ٤٨\n(And the people of the Heights will call out to some men) from the people of Hellfire who were of great status in the previous life, (whom they recognize by their marks, saying, \"Of no avail to you was your gathering) of wealth and children, (and [the fact] that you were arrogant) which kept you from accepting the faith. Al-Kalbi said: \"While on the Heights and looking at people of Hellfire, they will call some of them saying, O Walid bin Al-Mughera, O Abu Jahl bin Hisham. Then they will look at the side of Paradise and see (who used to be) the weak and poor people such as: Salman, Suhaib, Khabbab, and Bilal.\" Al-Baghawi: 2/106.\nThe criteria against which people are judged in the Hereafter are different from that of this worldly life. Explain. In light of this verse.\nأَهَٰٓؤُلَآءِ ٱلَّذِينَ أَقۡسَمۡتُمۡ لَا يَنَالُهُمُ ٱللَّهُ بِرَحۡمَةٍۚ\nThis is a statement of the people of the Heights to the people of Hellfire, and (these the ones) indicates the people of Paradise. That is because the disbelievers in this life swore that Allah would never offer mercy to the believers nor care for them, but the opposite will happen. Ibn Juzay: 1/360.\nExtract from this verse some causes for entering Hellfire?\nوَنَادَىٰٓ أَصۡحَٰبُ ٱلنَّارِ أَصۡحَٰبَ ٱلۡجَنَّةِ أَنۡ أَفِيضُواْ عَلَيۡنَا مِنَ ٱلۡمَآءِ أَوۡ مِمَّا رَزَقَكُمُ ٱللَّهُۚ قَالُوٓاْ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ حَرَّمَهُمَا عَلَى ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ٥٠\nThis verse proves that providing drinking water is one of the best deeds. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked: which charity is the best? He replied: Providing drinking water; do you not see when people of Hellfire will call the people of Paradise for help, they say, (Pour upon us some water or from whatever Allah has provided you). Some followers of the Prophet's companions said: \"Whoever committed many sins, then he should provide drinking water. If Allah has forgiven the sins of a man who provided water to a thirsty dog, then it is all the more so if one provides water to a believer.\" Al-Qurtubi: 9/233.\nDescribe the virtue of providing drinking water?\nوَنَادَىٰٓ أَصۡحَٰبُ ٱلنَّارِ أَصۡحَٰبَ ٱلۡجَنَّةِ أَنۡ أَفِيضُواْ عَلَيۡنَا مِنَ ٱلۡمَآءِ أَوۡ مِمَّا رَزَقَكُمُ ٱللَّهُۚ قَالُوٓاْ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ حَرَّمَهُمَا عَلَى ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ٥٠\nWhat is even worse for the disbelievers in this call is the fact that they can actually see the people of Paradise, which is far more disgracing and painful to them. Ibn Atiyah: 2/406.\nThe punishment in Hellfire is both physical and mental. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nحِجَابٌA barrier\nبِسِيمَاهُمBy their marks\nتِلقَاءَTurned towards\nأَصحَابُ الأَعرَافِPeople of the Heights [their good deeds and sins are equal]"],[157,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah humbly in private.\nWhen walking down a path, remove any obstacles or litter, and if you find something that is damaged and can be mended, then do it the best you can.\nThink of ways you can adopt to help you treat others with kindness and righteousness and ask Allah to be among the doers of good.\nguid\nGuidance, mercy, and knowledge are all in the Holy Book of Allah.\nBecoming a believer at the time of death or when facing Allah's punishment will not be of use, just as in the Hereafter.\nIf you seek Allah's mercy, then be a doer of good.\nrefl\nوَلَقَدۡ جِئۡنَٰهُم بِكِتَٰبٖ فَصَّلۡنَٰهُ عَلَىٰ عِلۡمٍ\n(Which We detailed by knowledge) from Allah, Who knows the situation of people at all times and in all places, and He knows what is and is not good for them. Hence, His explanation is not the explanation of one who is unaware of human affairs or ignorant of some of them, as a result of which he may issue an inappropriate ruling; rather, it is an explanation by One Whose knowledge encompasses all things and His mercy encompasses all things. Al-Saadi: 291.\nHow do you respond to the claim that Islamic Sharia does not fit present times?\nٱدۡعُواْ رَبَّكُمۡ تَضَرُّعٗا وَخُفۡيَةًۚ إِنَّهُۥ لَا يُحِبُّ ٱلۡمُعۡتَدِينَ ٥٥\nAccording to Sharia, performing voluntary acts of worship in private is better than performing them in public. Alhasan bin Abi Alhasan said: We have seen some people who always kept their voluntary good deeds private, and Muslims used to supplicate Allah diligently in an inaudible whisper. Al-Qurtubi: 9/244-245.\nWhich is better: performing voluntary acts of worship privately or in public?\nٱدۡعُواْ رَبَّكُمۡ تَضَرُّعٗا وَخُفۡيَةًۚ إِنَّهُۥ لَا يُحِبُّ ٱلۡمُعۡتَدِينَ ٥٥\nMeaning: Allah is saying to the people: Supplicate your Lord alone with sincerity, and never supplicate idols or false gods. (in humility): In submissiveness. (and privately) not by showing off while your hearts are uncertain of His Oneness and Lordship, as hypocrites would do. Al-Tabari: 12/485.\nWhat are the traits that should be observed when supplicating Allah?\nوَلَا تُفۡسِدُواْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ بَعۡدَ إِصۡلَٰحِهَا\nWhoever reflected on the lives of people in this world, would reach the conclusion that every goodness that they had enjoyed was due to observing the Oneness of Allah, His worship, and adherence to the teachings of His Messenger (ﷺ). On the other hand, every evil, trial, tribulation, drought, and defeat by an enemy are all due to disobedience of the Messenger (ﷺ) and the call to other than Allah. Ibn Taimyah: 3/170.\nWhat is the cause of every goodness on earth? What is the cause of every corruption on earth?\nوَٱدۡعُوهُ خَوۡفٗا وَطَمَعًاۚ إِنَّ رَحۡمَتَ ٱللَّهِ قَرِيبٞ مِّنَ ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ٥٦\nFear of Allah has three levels, first: A weak feeling that crosses the heart but has no real inward or outward effect on a person, therefore, this is a non-existent fear. Second: A strong feeling that awakens the person and induces him to become disciplined. Third: An extreme fear that pushes a person to despair and hopelessness, and this is prohibited. The middle level is the best one. When it comes to the fear of Allah, people have three states: Ordinary people's fear from the consequences of their sins; the elite's fear from the evil end of life, and the special elite's fear from what may occur based on the divine will and decree since the end of life depends on it. Ibn Juzay: 1/360.\nIn light of this verse, what is the best level of fear of Allah that one should observe?\nوَٱدۡعُوهُ خَوۡفٗا وَطَمَعًاۚ إِنَّ رَحۡمَتَ ٱللَّهِ قَرِيبٞ مِّنَ ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ٥٦\nthe necessary effort to attain it by doing good deeds and abstaining from sins, so this is the good hope. Second: Hoping, but with disobedience and sins, so this is a delusion. Third: Hope becomes too strong to the point of feeling completely safe, and this is prohibited. When it comes to hoping for Allah's mercy, people have three states: The hope of ordinary people for Allah's reward; the hope of the elite for Allah's Pleasure; the hope of the special elite to meet Allah out of yearning and love for Him. Ibn Juzay: 1/360.\nIn light of this verse, what is the appropriate level of hope for Allah’s mercy that one should observe?\nإِنَّ رَحۡمَتَ ٱللَّهِ قَرِيبٞ مِّنَ ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ٥٦\nThe doers of good are selected to be near Allah's mercy since He is the Most Merciful of the merciful, and His benevolence is for those who are benevolent, as a befitting recompense. And the more they do good, the more He rewards them with His mercy. Ibn Taimyah: 15/27.\nWhy are the doers of good selected to be near Allah's mercy?\nwords\nاستَوَىHe rose over\nحَثِيثًاRapidly\nوَخُفيَةًAnd privately\nأَقَلَّتIt Carried\nثِقَالًاHeavy [clouds]\nلِبَلَدٍTo a lifeless land"],[158,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nOffer thanks to Allah constantly with your heart, tongue, and through your deeds. Thanking Allah for his blessings is one of things that leads to increased knowledge, understanding, and faith.\nAsk Allah to save the oppressed believers and destroy the transgressing tyrants.\nRead up on matters crucial to your needs about the Oneness of Allah, and remind those around you about them.\nguid\nThe messages of the Prophets all coincide with the Oneness of Allah, thus hold fast to it through learning, teaching of others and practicing.\nThe misguided ones who seek benefits and authority often reject the Message of Allah, as it goes against their desires.\nIf a preacher attains these two traits, he will receive blessing and acceptance: Knowledge and sincere advice, thus, strive to attain them.\nrefl\nوَٱلۡبَلَدُ ٱلطَّيِّبُ يَخۡرُجُ نَبَاتُهُۥ بِإِذۡنِ رَبِّهِۦۖ وَٱلَّذِي خَبُثَ لَا يَخۡرُجُ إِلَّا نَكِدٗاۚ كَذَٰلِكَ نُصَرِّفُ ٱلۡأٓيَٰتِ لِقَوۡمٖ يَشۡكُرُونَ ٥٨\nThis is a likeness of hearts when revelation, which is the substance of life, just as rain is the substance of life, comes to them. When revelation comes to good hearts, they accept and learn it, and the result is in accordance with their good origin and good nature. As for evil hearts in which there is no good, when revelation comes to them it finds no acceptance; rather it finds these hearts negligent and heedless, or opposed to it. Hence, it is like rain that falls on a salty marsh, sand or rocks, and has no impact on them. Al-Saadi: 292.\nWhat are the types of hearts when receiving the revelation?\nقَالَ ٱلۡمَلَأُ مِن قَوۡمِهِۦٓ إِنَّا لَنَرَىٰكَ فِي ضَلَٰلٖ مُّبِينٖ ٦٠\n(The chiefs of his people said) means the general public, leaders, commanders and dignitaries of his people said, (We certainly see that you are clearly misguided) since you call on us to abandon the worship of these idols that we found our forefathers worshipping. This, indeed, is the attitude of evil people, for they consider the righteous people to be following misguidance as Allah says in other verses, (And when they saw them, they said: \"Indeed, these have gone astray\") [83:32], (And those who disbelieve say of those who believe: \"Had it been a good thing, they [the weak and poor] would not have preceded us thereto\") [46:11]. Ibn Kathir: 2/214.\nIn light of this verse, describe some of the trials faced by righteous people?\nقَالَ يَٰقَوۡمِ لَيۡسَ بِي ضَلَٰلَةٞ وَلَٰكِنِّي رَسُولٞ مِّن رَّبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٦١\nIn Noah's (peace be upon him) response to them, (I am not misguided), there is an extreme politeness, a turn away from their rudeness, a soft approach, and a breadth of mind, as the Prophetic moral character would merit. Ibn Atiyah: 2/415.\nThere is a lesson in Noah's (peace be upon him) response for those who call others to Allah. What is it?\nقَالَ يَٰقَوۡمِ لَيۡسَ بِي ضَلَٰلَةٞ وَلَٰكِنِّي رَسُولٞ مِّن رَّبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٦١ أُبَلِّغُكُمۡ رِسَٰلَٰتِ رَبِّي وَأَنصَحُ لَكُمۡ وَأَعۡلَمُ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ مَا لَا تَعۡلَمُونَ ٦٢\nThis is the quality of a Messenger; he conveys the Message using plain yet eloquent words, offers sincere advice and is knowledgeable about Allah. Ibn Kathir: 2/214.\nFor one who calls others to Allah, what qualities should he have?\nأُبَلِّغُكُمۡ رِسَٰلَٰتِ رَبِّي وَأَنصَحُ لَكُمۡ وَأَعۡلَمُ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ مَا لَا تَعۡلَمُونَ ٦٢\nMeaning: My role is to convey the message to you, to explain the Oneness of Allah, and His commands and prohibitions, by way of sincerity and compassion toward you. (And I know from Allah what you do not know), therefore what you ought to do is obey me and accept my advice, if you know. Al-Saadi: 293.\nIf the Messenger knows from Allah what his people do not, then what must they do?\nفَكَذَّبُوهُ فَأَنجَيۡنَٰهُ وَٱلَّذِينَ مَعَهُۥ فِي ٱلۡفُلۡكِ وَأَغۡرَقۡنَا ٱلَّذِينَ كَذَّبُواْ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَآۚ إِنَّهُمۡ كَانُواْ قَوۡمًا عَمِينَ ٦٤\nThe deliverance of the believers is mentioned first to show Allah's care for them, and to please the listening believers with His recurring way that whenever He destroys the disbelievers, He always saves the believers. Ibn Ashur: 8/197.\nIn this verse, the deliverance of the believers is mentioned first. Why?\nفَكَذَّبُوهُ فَأَنجَيۡنَٰهُ وَٱلَّذِينَ مَعَهُۥ فِي ٱلۡفُلۡكِ وَأَغۡرَقۡنَا ٱلَّذِينَ كَذَّبُواْ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَآۚ\nThis is Allah's way with His servants, in this life and the Hereafter, that the good end, victory and triumph is for those who fear Him, in the same way that He destroyed the people of Noah (peace be upon him), and saved him and his believing followers. Ibn Kathir: 2/214.\nThere is a lesson in the narrative of Noah (peace be upon him) for persecuted Muslims. What is it?\nwords\nنَكِدًاSparsely, with difficulty\nنُصَرِّفُWe diversify\nعَمِينَThey were blind [to the truth]\nسَفَاهَةٍFoolishness"],[159,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nConvey, with a nice approach, the message of Allah about a wrongdoing or a corruption that you encountered today.\nSit by yourself for some time and remind yourself of all the favors and blessings that Allah Has bestowed upon you.\nAsk Allah to save the oppressed Muslims in our times through His mercy and to eliminate the enemies of Islam with His Might.\nguid\nThe polytheists' argument that their acts of worship are valid because their ancestors were doing them is an ongoing habit of people of falsehood, and is part of a censured imitation.\nDemanding and seeking to hasten Allah's wrath is an indicator of the polytheists' extreme ignorance.\nEvery ruling or a statement with no evidence to support it is null.\nrefl\nأُبَلِّغُكُمۡ رِسَٰلَٰتِ رَبِّي وَأَنَا۠ لَكُمۡ نَاصِحٌ أَمِينٌ ٦٨\nThese, indeed, are the qualities of the Prophets: conveying, sincerity and honesty. Ibn Kathir: 2/215.\nWhat are the qualities that a preacher to Allah should have?\nوَٱذۡكُرُوٓاْ إِذۡ جَعَلَكُمۡ خُلَفَآءَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ قَوۡمِ نُوحٖ وَزَادَكُمۡ فِي ٱلۡخَلۡقِ بَصۜۡطَةٗۖ فَٱذۡكُرُوٓاْ ءَالَآءَ ٱللَّهِ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تُفۡلِحُونَ ٦٩\nProphet Hud (peace be upon him) shifted from reminding his people of the Oneness of Allah to reminding them of His favors upon them of which they did not deny He was the sole grantor since the creation and the command belong solely to Him, a reminder that would lead them to singling Him out for worship. Ibn Ashur: 8/204.\nThey were reminded of Allah's favors after that of His Oneness. Why?\nوَٱذۡكُرُوٓاْ إِذۡ جَعَلَكُمۡ خُلَفَآءَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ قَوۡمِ نُوحٖ وَزَادَكُمۡ فِي ٱلۡخَلۡقِ بَصۜۡطَةٗۖ فَٱذۡكُرُوٓاْ ءَالَآءَ ٱللَّهِ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تُفۡلِحُونَ ٦٩\nThis was a clear reminder of Allah's favors upon the people of Hud (peace be upon him), and an implicit warning not to follow the example of the people of Noah (peace be upon him), who were destroyed for their polytheism, as they (people of Hud) would face the same consequence if they do. Ibn Ashur: 8/205.\nIs it possible that a whole society can be punished? Explain in light of this verse.\nوَٱذۡكُرُوٓاْ إِذۡ جَعَلَكُمۡ خُلَفَآءَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ قَوۡمِ نُوحٖ\nMeaning: Remember when Allah made you successors to the people of Noah (peace be upon him), and praise your Lord and give thanks to Him, for He established you in the land and made you successors to the doomed nations who denied the Messengers, so Allah destroyed them, but He caused you to survive, to see what you will do. Beware of persisting in disbelief as they did, lest there befall you what befell them. Al-Saadi: 294.\nProphet Hud (peace be upon him) reminded his people of the fate of people of Noah (peace be upon him). Why?\nقَالُوٓاْ أَجِئۡتَنَا لِنَعۡبُدَ ٱللَّهَ وَحۡدَهُۥ وَنَذَرَ مَا كَانَ يَعۡبُدُ ءَابَآؤُنَا فَأۡتِنَا بِمَا تَعِدُنَآ إِن كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ ٧٠\nMay Allah curse them, for they regarded the beliefs and practices of their forefathers as the most important of obligations and the most perfect of matters, and something that no one should object to. They gave precedence to the misguidance of their forefathers, polytheism and idol worshiping over what the Messengers called to, namely affirming the Oneness of Allah, with no partner or associate. They rejected their Prophet and said: (Bring upon us what you are threatening us with, if you are truthful). Al-Saadi: 294.\nWhat should be the Muslim's attitude when his people's customs and traditions contradict Sharia rulings?\nقَالَ قَدۡ وَقَعَ عَلَيۡكُم مِّن رَّبِّكُمۡ رِجۡسٞ وَغَضَبٌۖ أَتُجَٰدِلُونَنِي فِيٓ أَسۡمَآءٖ سَمَّيۡتُمُوهَآ أَنتُمۡ وَءَابَآؤُكُم مَّا نَزَّلَ ٱللَّهُ بِهَا مِن سُلۡطَٰنٖۚ\n(You are definitely going to be subjected to the punishment and wrath of your Lord), it will inevitably befall you, for all the causes thereof are present and the time for doom has come. (Do you dispute with me concerning mere names that you and your forefathers have made up), how can you argue about matters that lack the truth, and about idols that you call gods, when there is nothing divine in them at all, not even an atom's weight. Al-Saadi: 294.\nHow could Prophet Hud (peace be upon him) say that torment had already fallen on them while it did not happen at that time yet?\nقَدۡ جَآءَتۡكُم بَيِّنَةٞ مِّن رَّبِّكُمۡۖ هَٰذِهِۦ نَاقَةُ ٱللَّهِ لَكُمۡ ءَايَةٗۖ فَذَرُوهَا تَأۡكُلۡ فِيٓ أَرۡضِ ٱللَّهِۖ وَلَا تَمَسُّوهَا بِسُوٓءٖ فَيَأۡخُذَكُمۡ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٞ ٧٣\n(A clear evidence from your Lord), a visible miracle which was the \"she-camel of Allah.\" It was called that to honor it, or because Allah created it without parents, as they suggested to their Prophet Saleh (peace be upon him) to have it come out of a stone, and they promised to accept his message if he did. So, the stone broke open and the she-camel came out while they were looking in awe, then it begot a baby camel, and some of them accepted Saleh's (peace be upon him) message while others did not. Ibn Juzay: 1/360.\nA misguided person argues and debates for the sake of the unattainable. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nبَسطَةًGreat stature\nآلاَءَ اللهِAllah's favors\nرِجسٌPunishment\nوَقَطَعنَا دَابِرَWe eliminated [them all]"],[160,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, make me love belief and adorn my heart with it. Make me hate disbelief, deviance, and rebellion, and place me among the rightly-guided.\"\nShare a message in which you warn others of arrogance and let them know that it may lead to shirk and disbelief.\nRecall one who has given you advice, thank and pray for him.\nguid\nBlessings recede with committing sins, thus keep away from them.\nLearn from someone living in a lesser condition than you, and do not shy away from accepting the truth from those below you.\nOne of the signs of impending doom is people's dislike of advice and advisors when they go against their desires.\nrefl\nوَبَوَّأَكُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ تَتَّخِذُونَ مِن سُهُولِهَا قُصُورٗا وَتَنۡحِتُونَ ٱلۡجِبَالَ بُيُوتٗاۖ فَٱذۡكُرُوٓاْ ءَالَآءَ ٱللَّهِ وَلَا تَعۡثَوۡاْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ مُفۡسِدِينَ ٧٤\nMeaning: Do not cause ruin to the earth with evildoing and sin, for sin leads to the ruin of civilization, and now their land is devoid of them and their dwellings are empty. Al-Saadi: 295.\nWhat are the effects of sins on favors?\nقَالَ ٱلۡمَلَأُ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱسۡتَكۡبَرُواْ مِن قَوۡمِهِۦ لِلَّذِينَ ٱسۡتُضۡعِفُواْ لِمَنۡ ءَامَنَ مِنۡهُمۡ أَتَعۡلَمُونَ أَنَّ صَٰلِحٗا مُّرۡسَلٞ مِّن رَّبِّهِۦۚ قَالُوٓاْ إِنَّا بِمَآ أُرۡسِلَ بِهِۦ مُؤۡمِنُونَ ٧٥\nThe arrogant chiefs switched from arguing with Prophet Saleh (peace be upon him) to testing the faith of his followers and casting doubts on it. Their argument with the followers was, in fact, an extension to their argument with Prophet Saleh (peace be upon him) himself. In this verse, they are described as arrogant to indicate their repulsive and humiliating attitude toward the rest of the people. Moreover, this indicates that the followers of Prophet Saleh (peace be upon him) are the weak among their people. Ibn Ashur: 8/222.\nIn light of this verse, explain how people of Saleh (peace be upon him) diversified their tactics to turn others away from his message.\nقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱسۡتَكۡبَرُوٓاْ إِنَّا بِٱلَّذِيٓ ءَامَنتُم بِهِۦ كَٰفِرُونَ ٧٦\nTheir arrogance made them defy the truth to which those who were regarded as weak had submitted. Al-Saadi: 295.\nIn light of this verse, describe one of the harms caused by arrogance?\nفَعَقَرُواْ ٱلنَّاقَةَ وَعَتَوۡاْ عَنۡ أَمۡرِ رَبِّهِمۡ وَقَالُواْ يَٰصَٰلِحُ ٱئۡتِنَا بِمَا تَعِدُنَآ إِن كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلِينَ ٧٧\n(So they killed the she-camel), the killing is attributed to all of them because they consented to it, even though it was carried out by one man only. Ibn Juzay: 1/360.\nThe killing is attributed to all of them even though it was done by one individual. Why?\nفَتَوَلَّىٰ عَنۡهُمۡ وَقَالَ يَٰقَوۡمِ لَقَدۡ أَبۡلَغۡتُكُمۡ رِسَالَةَ رَبِّي وَنَصَحۡتُ لَكُمۡ وَلَٰكِن لَّا تُحِبُّونَ ٱلنَّٰصِحِينَ ٧٩\n(But you do not like sincere advisers), since they favored to follow their desires over reason, the words of advice were hard for them to accept. Ibn Atiyah: 2/324.\nMost people do not like ones who give them advice. Why?\nوَلُوطًا إِذۡ قَالَ لِقَوۡمِهِۦٓ أَتَأۡتُونَ ٱلۡفَٰحِشَةَ مَا سَبَقَكُم بِهَا مِنۡ أَحَدٖ مِّنَ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٨٠\n(Do you commit such immorality), a behavior which surpasses, in its severity and abhorrent nature, all other shameful acts, (As no one has preceded you with from among the worlds). It was one of the most repulsive of acts and their invention of it, thus, setting a precedent for those who came after them, was also one of the most abhorrent of actions. Al-Saadi: 296.\nWhen does the guilt of a sin become multiplied? Explain in light of this verse.\nإِنَّكُمۡ لَتَأۡتُونَ ٱلرِّجَالَ شَهۡوَةٗ مِّن دُونِ ٱلنِّسَآءِۚ بَلۡ أَنتُمۡ قَوۡمٞ مُّسۡرِفُونَ ٨١\nThey transgressed in following their lustful desires, and therefore, they went on to try an abnormal desire when they became bored with the normal ones. Ibn Ashur: 8/232.\nWhy were the people of Lot (peace be upon him) described as (transgressing people)?\nwords\nوَبَوَّأَكُمHe Settled you and established for you\nوَلاَ تَعثَواDo not pursue\nفَعَقَرُواThey killed [the she-camel]\nوَعَتَواThey acted defiantly\nالرَّجفَةُAn overwhelming earthquake"],[161,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nRead the story of Shu'ayb and write down three useful lessons.\nRemind some sellers about the importance of being fair when using the scale.\nTalk to those who linger in the streets to harm others and advise them not to do that.\nguid\nIt is the habit of wrongdoers and crooked people that they turn the facts around; they disparage the righteous and praise the corrupt.\nAllah's religion has no favoritism toward anyone; When Lot's wife disobeyed, Allah tormented her along with the others.\nReflecting upon the consequences of the wrongdoers is a deterrent for one who contemplate to commit sins.\nrefl\nوَمَا كَانَ جَوَابَ قَوۡمِهِۦٓ إِلَّآ أَن قَالُوٓاْ أَخۡرِجُوهُم مِّن قَرۡيَتِكُمۡۖ إِنَّهُمۡ أُنَاسٞ يَتَطَهَّرُونَ ٨٢\nTheir saying, (Indeed, they are men who keep themselves pure) was making a mockery of them and their purity while they themselves were being proud of their heinous acts of shame. This is similar to some crooked men who would criticize a good person when he advises them, by saying: \"let us get away from this abstinent ,\" or \"remove this ascetic from here.\" Al-Qasimi: 5/139.\nWhat is the sign of reversed logic of some minds?\nوَمَا كَانَ جَوَابَ قَوۡمِهِۦٓ إِلَّآ أَن قَالُوٓاْ أَخۡرِجُوهُم مِّن قَرۡيَتِكُمۡۖ إِنَّهُمۡ أُنَاسٞ يَتَطَهَّرُونَ ٨٢\nIbn Al-Qayim said: Their saying, (Evict them from your city. Indeed, they are men who keep themselves pure) is similar to what Allah describes the makers of the Trench: (Their only grievance against them was that they believed in Allah, the All-Mighty, the Praiseworthy) [85:8]. As such is the polytheist whose only grievance against the believer is his devotion to the Oneness of Allah, and the religious innovator whose only grievance against the Sunni is his following of the Messenger (ﷺ) and not men's opinions. Hence, the patience of the follower of the Messenger (ﷺ) with the grievance of religious innovators is better, more useful, and easier than enduring the displeasure of Allah and His Messenger with those who follow the polytheists and religious innovators. Al-Qasimi: 5/141.\nHow does the believer counter the mockery of the disbelievers?\nفَأَوۡفُواْ ٱلۡكَيۡلَ وَٱلۡمِيزَانَ وَلَا تَبۡخَسُواْ ٱلنَّاسَ أَشۡيَآءَهُمۡ\nDefrauding is undervaluing goods by negative description to make them unattractive to others, and conning others out of the rightful weights and measures of their goods. All of that is considered as consuming people's wealth unlawfully, which is forbidden in all past nations by their Messengers (peace be upon them). Al-Qurtubi: 1/333.\nWhat is defrauding of property?\nوَلَا تُفۡسِدُواْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ بَعۡدَ إِصۡلَٰحِهَاۚ ذَٰلِكُمۡ خَيۡرٞ لَّكُمۡ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤۡمِنِينَ ٨٥\n(And do not spread corruption in the land), through disbelief and transgression. (After it has been set aright) after the Prophets and their righteous followers reformed its affairs with their Sharias by setting the just weights and measures, and prescribing legal punishments and rules. Al-Qasimi: 5/147.\nWhat is the worst type of corruption on earth?\nوَلَا تَقۡعُدُواْ بِكُلِّ صِرَٰطٖ تُوعِدُونَ وَتَصُدُّونَ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ مَنۡ ءَامَنَ بِهِۦ\n(And do not sit on every path, threatening), Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \"A path is a road to their city where they used to sit and turn people away from Prophet Shu'ayb (peace be upon him), saying that he was a liar so do not let him dissuade you from your religion.\" Al-Tabari: 12/557.\nThere are similarities between defaming tactics used against those who call others to Allah in the past and the present. Explain.\nوَلَا تَقۡعُدُواْ بِكُلِّ صِرَٰطٖ تُوعِدُونَ وَتَصُدُّونَ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ مَنۡ ءَامَنَ بِهِۦ وَتَبۡغُونَهَا عِوَجٗاۚ\nProphet Shu'ayb (peace be upon him) forbade his people from blocking the paths physically and in spiritual sense, saying, (And do not sit on every path, threatening), threatening people with death if they do not give up their money. (And averting from the way of Allah those who believe in Him, seeking to make it [seem] deviant), which means that you seek to make the path of Allah seem crooked and deviated. Ibn Kathir: 2/222.\nThere are two types of blocking a path. What are they?\nوَٱذۡكُرُوٓاْ إِذۡ كُنتُمۡ قَلِيلٗا فَكَثَّرَكُمۡۖ\nMeaning: Allah caused you to grow in number by blessing you with wives, offspring and good health, and He did not test you with epidemics or fatal diseases that would reduce your numbers, nor did He empower your enemies over you to eradicate you, nor caused you to be scattered in the land; rather, He blessed you by keeping you together, bestowing abundant provision on you and granting you numerous offspring. Al-Saadi: 296.\nThis verse indicates many blessings. Explain.\nwords\nالغَابِرِينَThose who remained in the torment\nوَلاَ تَبخَسُواDo not undervalue\nتُوعِدُونَThreatening to kill people\nوَتَبغُونَهَا عِوَجًاSeeking to make it crooked"],[162,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nShare a message, or remind those around you of some of the misfortunes that befell society, and that they will only be lifted through repentance and pleading humbly with Allah, the Almighty.\nSay, \"O Changer of the hearts, make my heart firm upon your religion.\"\nThank Allah for the blessings He bestowed upon you, and invoke Him that these blessings will not make you arrogant or distract you from obeying him.\nguid\nThe approach of arrogant people is the same: Arguing with falsehood, and when they fail, they resort to threats.\nWhen the desires of arrogant and heedless people conflict with the religion, they will follow their desires and become disobedient.\nOne should not be deluded by his faith and righteousness. Prophets and righteous men knew that their steadfastness in religion was only by Allah's will, not theirs.\nrefl\nقَالَ ٱلۡمَلَأُ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱسۡتَكۡبَرُواْ مِن قَوۡمِهِۦ\nMeaning: The nobles and prominent figures among them who followed their whims and desires and were preoccupied with their pleasures. When the truth came to them and they saw that it was not in accordance with their evil whims and desires, they rejected it and were too arrogant to follow it. Al-Saadi: 296.\nWhen one is deluded by pleasures, it may lead him to disbelief. How?\nقَالَ ٱلۡمَلَأُ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱسۡتَكۡبَرُواْ مِن قَوۡمِهِۦ لَنُخۡرِجَنَّكَ يَٰشُعَيۡبُ وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ مَعَكَ مِن قَرۡيَتِنَآ أَوۡ لَتَعُودُنَّ فِي مِلَّتِنَاۚ قَالَ أَوَلَوۡ كُنَّا كَٰرِهِينَ ٨٨\nFor the unwilling, complying with the religion does not serve its intended purpose, which is purifying the soul, increasing the number of devout followers, and attaining the required righteousness. Ibn Ashur: 9/7.\nFor the unwilling, complying with the religion does not serve its intended purposes. Explain In light of this verse.\nفَأَخَذَتۡهُمُ ٱلرَّجۡفَةُ\nAllah says that the earthquake shook them as a punishment for threatening to expel Shu'ayb and his followers. Ibn Kathir: 2/223.\nWhat is correlation between the punishment of people of Madyan and their stance on Shu'ayb (peace be upon him)?\nٱلَّذِينَ كَذَّبُواْ شُعَيۡبٗا كَأَن لَّمۡ يَغۡنَوۡاْ فِيهَاۚ\nMeaning: After the torment seized them, it looked as if they had never dwelled in the land from which they wanted to expel their Messenger Shu'ayb (peace be upon him) and his followers. Ibn Kathir: 2/223.\nIn light of this verse, talk about this rule: (The requital befits the action).\nفَكَيۡفَ ءَاسَىٰ عَلَىٰ قَوۡمٖ كَٰفِرِينَ ٩٣\nMeaning: I mourn. Al-Qurtubi: 9/287.\nShould the Muslim mourn the demise of the disbelievers?\nوَمَآ أَرۡسَلۡنَا فِي قَرۡيَةٖ مِّن نَّبِيٍّ إِلَّآ أَخَذۡنَآ أَهۡلَهَا بِٱلۡبَأۡسَآءِ وَٱلضَّرَّآءِ لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَضَّرَّعُونَ ٩٤\nThis verse and others in the Quran, as well as the history of religions reveal that the Messengers were sent to the people who lived in the cities rather than those who lived in rural areas to indicate that the aim of sending Allah's Messengers was to disseminate righteousness to the people of developed societies which are subject to flaws due to the mixing of contrasting groups. Moreover, those who live in rural areas are influenced by the people of nearby cities, as they rely on them for their different needs. Ibn Ashur: 9/16.\nWhat is wisdom behind sending Messengers to city people rather than people in rural areas?\nثُمَّ بَدَّلۡنَا مَكَانَ ٱلسَّيِّئَةِ ٱلۡحَسَنَةَ حَتَّىٰ عَفَواْ وَّقَالُواْ قَدۡ مَسَّ ءَابَآءَنَا ٱلضَّرَّآءُ وَٱلسَّرَّآءُ فَأَخَذۡنَٰهُم بَغۡتَةٗ وَهُمۡ لَا يَشۡعُرُونَ ٩٥\n(Then We changed their adversity into prosperity) means that We have replaced poverty and hardship with prosperity, testing them in both cases. (Until they increased [and flourished]) they increased in number and prospered in wealth. (And said, \"Our forefathers were also afflicted with hardship and ease\") this happened to our fathers and did not harm them because it is a coincidental event, not a test. Ibn Juzay: 1/360.\nAllah tests people with both prosperity and hardship, but they are not admonished. Why? Does this apply to some of the situations at the present times?\nwords\nالرَّجفَةُSevere/extreme earthquake\nجَاثِمِينَThey perished, stuck to the ground on their knees and faces\nآسَىI grieve"],[163,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nDeliver a speech or share a message in which you make clear that the solution to the problems of society is cooperation in avoiding sins and believing in Allah's promise and threat.\nChoose a city or a tribe whose story is mentioned in the Quran, and collect its narratives from the whole Quran to reflect on it.\nKeep praying in congregation, as it is part of the covenant between you and Allah.\nguid\nWhen the community feel secure from the plan of Allah, then it stands ready for its demise.\nThe tribulation and hardship which afflict you are consequences of your sins and shortcomings.\nOne of the greatest misfortunes is when the heart is sealed over so that it does not perceive good nor desist from evil.\nrefl\nوَلَوۡ أَنَّ أَهۡلَ ٱلۡقُرَىٰٓ ءَامَنُواْ وَٱتَّقَوۡاْ لَفَتَحۡنَا عَلَيۡهِم بَرَكَٰتٖ مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَلَٰكِن كَذَّبُواْ فَأَخَذۡنَٰهُم بِمَا كَانُواْ يَكۡسِبُونَ ٩٦\nblessings from the heaven and earth) this indicates that blessings which people enjoy come either from earth mostly, or from heaven, such as rain, rays of the sun, light of the moon, the stars, air and good winds. Ibn Ashur: 9/22.\nBlessings for the people come from either the heaven or earth. Explain.\nوَلَوۡ أَنَّ أَهۡلَ ٱلۡقُرَىٰٓ ءَامَنُواْ وَٱتَّقَوۡاْ لَفَتَحۡنَا عَلَيۡهِم بَرَكَٰتٖ مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ\nIf the people of the cities had believed sincerely in their hearts, which was confirmed by righteous deeds, and they had actually feared Allah both outwardly and inwardly, by giving up what Allah had prohibited, He would have bestowed upon them the blessings of heaven and earth. Al-Saadi: 298.\nHow does the livelihood of people of cities and villages become prosperous?\nأَفَأَمِنُواْ مَكۡرَ ٱللَّهِۚ فَلَا يَأۡمَنُ مَكۡرَ ٱللَّهِ إِلَّا ٱلۡقَوۡمُ ٱلۡخَٰسِرُونَ ٩٩\nThe plan of Allah and His gradual leading of them to their destruction is through what He bestowed upon them of the blessings in this life. Al-Baghawi: 2/132.\nWhat is meant by the plan of Allah in this verse?\nفَلَا يَأۡمَنُ مَكۡرَ ٱللَّهِ إِلَّا ٱلۡقَوۡمُ ٱلۡخَٰسِرُونَ ٩٩\nThis verse is intended to instill a great deal of fear, so that the individual should never feel safe from losing his faith. Rather, he should always be worried and anxious, lest he go through the trials that deprive him of his faith. Al-Saadi: 298.\nFor one who is reflecting on this verse, what should he do?\nفَلَا يَأۡمَنُ مَكۡرَ ٱللَّهِ إِلَّا ٱلۡقَوۡمُ ٱلۡخَٰسِرُونَ ٩٩\nAl-Hasan Al-Basri said: \"The believer performs acts of worship, all the while feeling fear, in fright and anxiety; the wicked sinner commits sins while feeling safe [from Allah's punishment]. Ibn Kathir: 2/224.\nWhat is the difference between the believer and the disbeliever toward feeling secure from the plan of Allah?\nأَوَ لَمۡ يَهۡدِ لِلَّذِينَ يَرِثُونَ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ أَهۡلِهَآ أَن لَّوۡ نَشَآءُ أَصَبۡنَٰهُم بِذُنُوبِهِمۡۚ وَنَطۡبَعُ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمۡ فَهُمۡ لَا يَسۡمَعُونَ ١٠٠\n(We seal over their hearts so they do not hear), if Allah alerts them but they do not respond, reminds them but they pay no heed, and shows them signs but they are not guided, then Allah will punish them and place a seal on their hearts, topped with stain and impurities until they are blocked. Then, no truth or goodness can reach them, and they cannot hear what benefits them; rather they hear what establishes proof against them. Al-Saadi: 298.\nWhat is the severest punishment, in this life, for those who turn away from the religion of Allah?\nفَٱنظُرۡ كَيۡفَ كَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلۡمُفۡسِدِينَ ١٠٣\nMeaning: Look, O Muhammad, how We punished them, We caused them to drown, all of them, while Moses (peace be upon him) and his people were watching. Public drowning added disgrace to the punishment that Pharaoh and his people suffered, while adding comfort to the hearts of the allies of Allah, Moses (peace be upon him) and those who believed in him. Ibn Kathir: 2/225-226.\nWhat is the wisdom behind commanding to reflect on the demise of the disbelievers?\nwords\nبَأسُنَاOur punishment\nبَيَاتًاAt night\nأَوَلَم يَهدِHas it not become clear\nيَرِثُونَThose who inherit\nوَنَطبَعُWe seal over [their hearts]"],[164,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nStart a project, or a campaign, where you defend oppressed people and help the persecuted.\nAsk Allah to guide you to obey Him, and to be among the supporters of the truth.\nShare a video clip of a lecture that brings to light the risk of witchcraft.\nguid\nIt is easy to deceive a community which is ignorant of the truth.\nThe chiefs falsely accused Prophet Moses of seeking power, but in reality, he wanted to guide people to worshiping Allah alone.\nNo matter how much falsehood spreads and rises, and the impatient ones are deceived by it, there will be a day when the truth appears and rises.\nrefl\nفَأَلۡقَىٰ عَصَاهُ فَإِذَا هِيَ ثُعۡبَانٞ مُّبِينٞ ١٠٧ وَنَزَعَ يَدَهُۥ فَإِذَا هِيَ بَيۡضَآءُ لِلنَّٰظِرِينَ ١٠٨ قَالَ ٱلۡمَلَأُ مِن قَوۡمِ فِرۡعَوۡنَ إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَسَٰحِرٌ عَلِيمٞ ١٠٩\nMoses (threw his staff) onto the ground, (and it suddenly became a real serpent) a visible snake as they were looking on. (And he drew out his hand) from his collar (and it was shining white to the beholders) without harm. These were two great signs that highlighted the truth of the message that Moses brought, which proved that he was indeed a Messenger of the Lord of the worlds. But those who do not believe, even if all signs come to them, will not believe until they see the painful punishment. Al-Saadi: 299.\nIs reason enough to reach true guidance? Or is true guidance a favor from Allah? Explain in light of these verses.\nقَالُوٓاْ أَرۡجِهۡ وَأَخَاهُ وَأَرۡسِلۡ فِي ٱلۡمَدَآئِنِ حَٰشِرِينَ ١١١ يَأۡتُوكَ بِكُلِّ سَٰحِرٍ عَلِيمٖ ١١٢\nSince the eminent among the people of Pharaoh were reasonable and politically sensible, they knew that the Message brought by Moses became known to the people, and that if Pharaoh imprisoned Moses or acted in a stubborn way, then the people would realize that Moses' argument had won, which would cast doubts on Pharaoh's religion. Hence, they suggested a softer approach in dealing with Moses in the hope of finding among Egypt's magicians someone who could refute the signs of Moses, and so the argument would visibly become against him before all people. Ibn Ashur: 9/44.\nThe eminent among the people of Pharaoh did not suggest imprisoning Moses (peace be upon him). Why?\nوَجَآءَ ٱلسَّحَرَةُ فِرۡعَوۡنَ قَالُوٓاْ إِنَّ لَنَا لَأَجۡرًا إِن كُنَّا نَحۡنُ ٱلۡغَٰلِبِينَ ١١٣\n(And said) they said to Pharaoh, (Will we have a reward), which is a prize money. Al-Baghawi: 2/135.\nThis verse unveils one of the most important traits of those who misguide others, which is their greed for worldly gains. How?\nوَجَآءَ ٱلسَّحَرَةُ فِرۡعَوۡنَ قَالُوٓاْ إِنَّ لَنَا لَأَجۡرًا إِن كُنَّا نَحۡنُ ٱلۡغَٰلِبِينَ ١١٣ قَالَ نَعَمۡ وَإِنَّكُمۡ لَمِنَ ٱلۡمُقَرَّبِينَ ١١٤\nWhen the magicians said to Pharaoh: Will we have a reward if we prevail over Moses, he said: Yes, and you will be among those who are near me. Al-Tabari: 13/26.\nIn this verse, there is a reference to tyrants who are keen on bringing closer to them the leaders of misguidance and consult them?\nقَالُواْ يَٰمُوسَىٰٓ إِمَّآ أَن تُلۡقِيَ وَإِمَّآ أَن نَّكُونَ نَحۡنُ ٱلۡمُلۡقِينَ ١١٥ قَالَ أَلۡقُواْۖ\nIt is said that the wisdom behind asking them to throw first, is that -and Allah knows best- the people might witness the magicians' sorcery first. When the magicians had cast their spell and captured the eyes, the clear and unequivocal truth came, at a time when they all anticipated and waited for it to come so it would even more impressive to their hearts, and that is what happened. Ibn Kathir: 2/227.\nWhat is the wisdom behind asking them to throw first?\nقَالُواْ يَٰمُوسَىٰٓ إِمَّآ أَن تُلۡقِيَ وَإِمَّآ أَن نَّكُونَ نَحۡنُ ٱلۡمُلۡقِينَ ١١٥ قَالَ أَلۡقُواْۖ فَلَمَّآ أَلۡقَوۡاْ سَحَرُوٓاْ أَعۡيُنَ ٱلنَّاسِ وَٱسۡتَرۡهَبُوهُمۡ وَجَآءُو بِسِحۡرٍ عَظِيمٖ ١١٦\nThe magicians showed respect for Moses (peace be upon him), and this became a cause for them to become believers. Al-Qurtubi: 9/296.\nIn light of this verse, explain the benefit of showing respect for the scholars and righteous people.\nوَأُلۡقِيَ ٱلسَّحَرَةُ سَٰجِدِينَ ١٢٠\nThe people for whom truth became clearest were the people of magic who knew all types of magic and the details thereof, which other people did not. Hence, they realized that this was a great sign, one of the signs of Allah that no human could produce. Al-Saadi: 300.\nWhy did the magicians become believers before anyone else during this event?\nwords\nحَقِيقٌI am obliged\nثُعبَانٌ مُبِينٌA real serpent\nوَنَزَعَ يَدَهُAnd he drew out his hand [out of his collar]\nأَرجِهLet him wait\nوَاستَرهَبُوهُمAnd they struck terror into them\nوَانقَلَبُواAnd became\nصَاغِرِينَUtterly humiliated"]])